WEBVTT

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:46.100
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Guys, for

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:50.820
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: the arrival of the Senate President, the Presiding Officer of the Impeachment Court, and the Senator Judges.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:34.700
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Sergeant-at-Arms is directed to make a proclamation.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:45.680
Alfredo Sotto Corpuz: All persons are commanded to keep silent under pain of penalty while the Impeachment Court is in session for the trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:56.120
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Impeachment Trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte is hereby called to order. We shall be led in prayer by Senator Judge Panfilo Lacson.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:07.460
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: Let us all pause for one minute of silent prayer for humility, wisdom, neutrality, and fairness.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:20.340
Sen. Panfilo “Ping” M. Lacson: In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit. Amen. Amen.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:23.580
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Clerk of Court will now call the roll.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:09:15.910
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Roll call of members. The Honorable Senator Judge Aquino, Senator Judge Cayetano Allan, Senator Judge Cayetano Pia, Senator Judge De La Rosa, Atty. Ersito, Atty. Goh, Atty. Ontiveros, Atty. Lacson, Atty. Lapid, Atty. Legarda, Atty. Marcoleta, Atty. Marcos, Atty. Padilla, Atty. Pangilinan, Atty. Soto III, Atty. Tulfo Erwin, Atty. Raffi, Atty. Villanueva Setor Judge Villar Camille, Setor Judge Villar Marc, Setor Judge Zubiri, The Presiding Officer Setor Judge Escudero, Senate President De Chalian.

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:31.360
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: With 20 senators present, the Chair declares the presence of a quorum. In accordance with the rules of procedure on impeachment trials, the Chair now recognizes the newly elected Presiding Officer to preside over the proceedings of the Impeachment Court.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.420
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you Mr. Senate President.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:10:49.990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The chair would like to defer action or approval on the journal as we await the manifestations of some of our senator judges. However, having said that, before we end today's trial, regardless of the submission of the senator judges who manifested their intention to submit their manifestations, we will have to approve the journal already so that we can furnish the parties with a copy As requested by council for the respondents, they would want an official copy of yesterday's ruling in order to afford them sufficient time to avail of whatever remedies they may want to seek in regard to the ruling in whole or in part. So for the information of the council for the parties, we shall be approving the journal within the day. You shall have a copy of the same before today's trial ends. This is also to inform the senator judges to make their submissions At the soonest possible time otherwise it shall only be made part of the transcript and the records and will no longer be made part of the journal so ordered and for the information of the body the clerk of court will please call the

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:57.450
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Case No. 004-2026, in the matter of the Impeachment Trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.550
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: appearances of the parties please good

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:10.070
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: afternoon your honors same appearance for the prosecution We are ready for the presentation of our next witness, Your Honor.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:15.690
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Appearances for the respondent. Good afternoon, Your Honors. Same appearance for the defense.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:27.930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: May we know who on the part of the counsel, rather, who among the panel of prosecutors or counsel from the panel of prosecutors will be presenting the witness?

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:32.190
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: This representation, Your Honor, will be presenting the next witness.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:37.990
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: May I know, likewise, on the part of the counsel for respondents, who will be standing on the other side? Will it be

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:38.530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: you, Atty. Villanueva?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:39.910
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: That's correct, Your Honor.

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:44.890
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed. Lead Prosecutor, call your first witness.

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:57.890
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honors, we are calling to the witness stand our next witness, the last witness for Article IV, Threat, Atty. Melvin Matibag, NBI Director.

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:56.350
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly remain standing, Director Matibag. The clerk will kindly administer the oath to the witness.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:03.470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly turn on the mic of the clerk of court. You, Melvin

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:19.750
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Melvin A. Matibag, do you swear that the evidence you shall give in the case now pending between the Philippines and Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte shall be the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth, so help you God?

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:20.510
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes, sir.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:22.950
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Kindly sit down, Director Matibag.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:34.250
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before the lead prosecutor proceeds with their direct examinations, the chair would like to address the witness regarding certain matters.

00:13:36.020 --> 00:14:43.140
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Director Matibag, the chair would like to remind and admonish you on behalf of the impeachment court to kindly avoid statements appertaining to individual members of this impeachment court. Without prejudice to any investigation you are undertaking, you may do so. But without need of issuing statements that may impinge upon the independence and or integrity of the court or the individual senator judges. And for this reason, for your information as well, Atty. Director Matibag, the statements made by Senators, Senator Judge Alan Peter Cayetano and Senator Judge Pia Cayetano last July 15 pertaining to statements made by you and the video presented in the impeachment court shall be referred to the Senate as a legislative body and referred to the appropriate committee, specifically the Rules Committee, for its proper disposition and for the matter to be taken up thereat and not in this impeachment court. I hope you will adhere and understand, Director Matibag, the reminder and the admonition of the Chair.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:44.260
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes, Your Honor.

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:50.100
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Director Matibag. Lead Prosecutor, the Honorable Luistro, you may proceed with your direct examination.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:15:22.020
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor. We are offering the testimony of witness, NBI Director, Atty. Melvin Matibag, to prove the following. One, siya ang kasalukuyang director ng National Bureau of Investigation. Two, matapos siyang italaga bilang director, may binuo siyang Special Task Force para magsagawa ng investigasyon.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:26.900
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: 3.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:52.500
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: May karagdagang investigasyon na isinagawa ang Special Task Force hinggil sa mga pagbabantang ginawa sa buhay ng Pangulo kasama ang pagbabanta ng Vice Presidente. 4. Ang pagbanta sa buhay ng Pangulo ay hindi lamang pagbanta sa kanyang buhay.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.760
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: 5.

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:23.030
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Ang mga natuklasan at naging risulta ng Special Task Force mula sa karagdagang imbistigasyon 6. Kilalanin at patunayan ang mga dokumento kaugnay ng nasabing imbistigasyon ng NBI 7. Ang iba pang mga bagay

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:33.540
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Comments, Your Honor.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:18:28.100
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, as to the first purpose, we are willing to stipulate, Your Honor, that Atty. Matib is the current NBI Director. In the interest of expediting the proceedings, no need to propound questions on that. Number two, as to the task force, Your Honor, we would have to object. On the basis of them being irrelevant, your honor would just like to manifest for the record that such task force, your honor, was not part of the articles of impeachment as well as the impeachment complaint. There was no mention thereof, and this is tantamount to a new information. So your honor would just like to manifest for the record that the articles of impeachment is Akin to a information that is filed in court and the trials already started and the prosecution cannot modify such information or articles of impeachment for such will be a violation of our client's right to due process particularly her right to be promptly and fully apprised of the exact charge against her so any information any new information is irrelevant number three Same objection, Your Honor, because the Good Counsel mentioned karagdagang investigation. So it pertains also to a new information which is irrelevant. Number four, we would have to object because the Good Counsel used the word banta, which is a conclusion of fact. She mentioned it twice. So we are objecting on the basis of it being conclusions of fact. Number 5, as to the special task force, same objection, Your Honor, considering that, again, there was no mention of such information, new information in the articles of impeachment. Numbers 6 and 7 are okay, Your Honor.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Would the lead prosecutor care to respond?

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:35.030
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: We would like to respond, Your Honor.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.150
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The lady may proceed.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:38.950
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor,

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:58.250
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Later,

00:19:04.890 --> 00:20:12.140
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, we will present that this Special Task Force was specifically created For the purpose of furthering the investigation because of the possibility of seeing na hindi po mag-isa ang vicepresidente sa bantang ito. In other words, Your Honor, the mention of special task force including its creation at ang karagdagang investigasyon nito passes the test. As a matter of fact, this is the very reason why we are presenting Atty. Melvin Matibag, the NBI Director before the Honorable Impeachment Court. Your Honor, the defense likewise mentioned that Special Task Force was not mentioned in the articles of impeachment.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:46.490
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: The decision of the Impeachment Court yesterday was based on documents which pertain to acts and omissions prior to 2022 and acts or omissions which were not specifically mentioned in the articles of impeachment. What is important here, Your Honor, are the allegations or testimonies to be presented.

00:20:52.090 --> 00:21:47.640
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: It is not necessary that they be specifically mentioned in the articles of impeachment. Finally, Your Honor, they likewise raise the issue of due process of the respondent. It is very much apparent, Your Honor, since day one of our impeachment trial, the respondent is very well represented by her very much able defense panel. In other words, Your Honor, atin pong ibinibigay ang nararapat na due process sa Respondent Vice President. And as far as this impeachment trial is concerned, kasama na po ang pagtistigo ni NBI Director kaugnay ng Special Task Force and all those who were involved in this investigation.

00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:40.330
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Chair reminds the lead prosecutor to skip the introduction and preliminary questions with respect to the witness being the current NBI director, having been admitted by the counsel for respondent. Insofar as the phrase banta is concerned, Chair would like to remind the senator judges that that is indeed a conclusion which the prosecutors will seek to prove for our purposes.

00:22:42.630 --> 00:23:37.460
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tawagin na lamang natin o ituring na lamang natin ang mga pahayag ang binitiwan ng ikalawang Pangulo. But Lead Prosecutor, kindly let the witness testify and characterize it as such if he will, but it should come from the witness and not from any of the counsel for the parties. As to the task force, the task force was formed on April 16, 2026 after the impeachment complaints have been filed. Although the impeachment complaint was filed before the Senate in May, the impeachment complaints were already filed prior to the formation of the task force. And as a last point, this, if at all, would show persistence, absence or lack of it, which is an element of the crime of grave threats which the prosecution is seeking to prove. Again, not through their statements, but through the witnesses they will be presenting in the person today.

00:23:39.700 --> 00:24:09.960
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The Chair will therefore allow the testimony and the counsel for the respondent may object at any time with respect to the points he raised in the Chair will rule. Each time an objection is raised regarding that matter without prejudice. I'm already seeing what Atty. Vinluan will do because he's reaching for the mic. Without prejudice to the counsel of course making a continuing objection with respect to his observations to the offer. So that we would abbreviate the proceedings and we won't need to object each time if at all it is brought up. Would that be correct, attorney?

00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:15.320
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yes, Your Honor. We register our continuing objection and everything subject to cross-examination.

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:19.100
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Noted. The lead prosecutor may proceed. Your witness.

00:24:21.680 --> 00:24:28.460
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Mr. Witness, please state your name, age, and other details.

00:24:30.020 --> 00:24:44.960
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ako po si Atty. Melvin Matibag, na kasalukuyang Director ng National Bureau of Investigation. Ang amin pong tanggapan ay may address na 9th floor, Filinvest Cyberzone Bay, Building C, Diosdado Macapagal Boulevard, Pasay City.

00:24:45.810 --> 00:24:54.260
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Nabanggit mo na ikaw ay isang abogado. Gaano ka na katagal sa nasabing propesyon?

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:56.060
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 29 years po.

00:24:58.680 --> 00:25:02.020
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Saan ka nagtapos ng iyong abogasya?

00:25:02.520 --> 00:25:04.460
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa Ateneo Law School po.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:11.700
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Bago ang iyong abogasya, ano ang una mong inaral sa kolehiyo?

00:25:11.960 --> 00:25:18.340
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ako po ay nagtapos ng Bachelor of Arts, Major in Philosophy, sa University of Santo Tomas.

00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:25.940
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Pagkatapos naman ng abogasya, Mr. Witness, ano ang iyong inaral kung mayroon man?

00:25:26.280 --> 00:25:33.830
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Nag-aral po ako ng Masters of Law, Major in Corporate and Finance Law, sa Wayne State University, Detroit, Michigan, USA po.

00:25:36.160 --> 00:25:54.310
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: You are here as NBI Director. Bago ka itinalaga bilang NBI Director, ano ang iyong mga naging trabaho, kung mayroon man?

00:25:54.320 --> 00:26:02.350
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Bago po ako itinalaga bilang NBI Director ay kasalukuyan po akong naglilingkod bilang dean o dekano ng Lyceum of Alabang College of Law.

00:26:02.360 --> 00:26:23.030
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Nabanggit mo na ikaw ay dating dean ng Lyceum of Alabang College of Law. Bukod sa pagiging dean, ano pa, kung mayroon man, ang iyong naging trabaho bago ang iyong pagkatalaga bilang NBI Director?

00:26:23.040 --> 00:26:37.870
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ako po ay nanungkulan na rin sa iba't ibang kapasidad sa ilalim po ng iba't ibang administrasyon. Una-una po rito, bilang director ng Laguna Lake Development Authority sa administrasyon po ng dating Pangulong Gloria Macapagal-Arroyo.

00:26:37.880 --> 00:27:03.950
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Nabanggit mo na ikaw ay naglingkod bilang director ng Laguna Lake Development Authority panahon ng dating Pangulong Gloria Macapagal-Arroyo. Ano pa, Mr. Witness, kung mayroon man, ang iyong naging trabaho bago ka itinalaga bilang NBI Director?

00:27:03.960 --> 00:27:18.920
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa administrasyon po ng dating Pangulong Gloria Macapagal-Arroyo, ako rin po ay nanungkulan bilang General Manager ng Manila International Airport Authority. At sa administrasyon din po ng dating Pangulong Rodrigo Roa Duterte, ako rin po ay nanungkulan sa iba't ibang kapasidad po.

00:27:19.080 --> 00:27:32.870
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: mentioned that under the administration of President Duterte, you also served in the government. Ano itong mga posisyon mo sa gobyerno na iyong nabanggit?

00:27:32.990 --> 00:27:34.390
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Relevance.

00:27:35.160 --> 00:27:38.320
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, may I respond? Counsel may answer.

00:27:38.940 --> 00:27:40.280
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel may respond, rather.

00:27:40.440 --> 00:27:59.240
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: The prosecution, Your Honor, is establishing the competence of the witness, the qualification as an official of the government. We are establishing, Your Honor, that he is loyal to his duty. Regardless of the principal, he is serving.

00:27:59.600 --> 00:28:03.960
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Wind up with your preliminaries, Council. Witness may answer. Objection overruled.

00:28:03.980 --> 00:28:22.340
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Thank you, Your Honor. I have been appointed as President and CEO of National Transmission Corporation from January 2017 until March 2022. After that, I was appointed as Cabinet Secretary of former President Rodrigo Roa Duterte.

00:28:29.120 --> 00:28:30.340
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Mr.

00:28:38.160 --> 00:28:47.860
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Witness, Bilang NBI Director, ano ang iyong mga responsibilidad at kapangyarihan?

00:28:54.030 --> 00:28:54.990
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Director, Your Honor.

00:28:55.130 --> 00:29:01.030
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Did you stipulate, counsel, as well as with the powers and responsibilities of—

00:29:01.030 --> 00:29:04.630
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We're willing to stipulate, Your Honor, as what the law provides.

00:29:05.530 --> 00:29:39.080
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, regardless of the position of the defense to stipulate on the fact pertaining to the powers and responsibilities of the NBI Director, it is the position of the prosecution that since this is a constitutional process, Mahalaga po na marinig ng ating mga iginagalang na senator judges. Ganon din ng mga kababayang nanonood kung ano talaga ang responsibilidad at kapangyarihan ng isang NBI director.

00:29:39.560 --> 00:29:55.230
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Understood, counsel. But it has been stipulated already by counsel for the respondents. So kindly go straight to the matter at the soonest possible time. You're in a short leash with respect to the preliminaries on the qualifications of the witness. Kindly proceed, ma'am.

00:29:57.530 --> 00:29:58.230
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Mr. Witness?

00:30:00.500 --> 00:30:05.620
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Ano ang iyong mga kapangyarihan at responsibilidad kung iyong nalalaman?

00:30:06.380 --> 00:30:35.120
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang kasama po rito sa aking mga responsibilidad, ang una-una na po, we are the primary investigating authority ng ating pong mansa. Kung kaya po, ito po ay aming mandato na mag-imbestiga sa anumang usapin o mga maaaring kribe na pumapasok sa amin. At kasama rin po rito ang pagbabalangkas ng mga pulisiya. Pagbubuo ng mga units or divisions kung kinakailangan at ang pag-management po administratively po ng aming opisina.

00:30:35.400 --> 00:30:47.480
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Sa mga kapangyarihan at responsibilidad na iyong binanggit, ano ang araw-araw mong ginagampanan, kung mayroon man at kung iyong nalalaman?

00:30:48.080 --> 00:30:59.110
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang araw-araw pong pagbabantay at pakikipag-ugnayan sa aming mga ahente dahil po sa araw-araw naming pag-ibistiga. Ang iba't iba pong usapin na pumapasok po sa aming ahensya.

00:31:00.110 --> 00:31:12.510
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Kaugnay pa rin ng mga binanggit mong kapagyarihan at responsibilidad. Ano ang pinakamabigat mo na responsibilidad bilang NBI Director kung iyong nalalaman?

00:31:12.590 --> 00:31:13.890
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Objection, Your Honor. Calls for an opinion.

00:31:15.320 --> 00:31:18.720
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Witness may answer. I think witness is competent enough to answer that question.

00:31:19.260 --> 00:31:52.240
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Ang akin pong hindi lamang po bilang primary investigating agency kundi ang aming pong primerong ginagawa ay ang pagbabantay para po sa ating mga taong bayan at bantayan din po na ang ating konstitusyon ay may patupad at siguraduhin na hindi po nagkakaroon ng kaguluhan at ligalig para po ito po ay puksain, habulin at amin pong Ang mga taong lumalabag po sa aming pong mandatong binabantayan.

00:32:29.940 --> 00:32:41.660
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Bukod sa ang respondent ay ang vicepresidente, ano pa kung mayroon man ang pagkakakinanlan ng respondent sa impeachment trial na ito?

00:32:42.710 --> 00:33:15.230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Basi po sa aking mandato bilang director nang ako po ay pumasok sa abing opisina, lahat po ng mga kasong nakabimbin at mga amin na naipasok sa Department of Justice ay akin pong nirebisa at tinignan upang akin po itong masubaybayan. At isa po sa mga kasong aking nakita rito, ang respondent po rito ay ang ating pong vicepresidente kung saan po siya ay kinasuhan ng aming Cybercrime Division ng Grave threat at inciting to sedition na sa kasalukuyan po ngayong nakabindihin sa Department of Justice.

00:33:16.090 --> 00:33:30.830
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Nabanggit mo na ang respondent ay may kasong grave threat at inciting to sedition sa DOJ? Mr. Witness, ano pa kung mayroon man ang pagkakakilanlan ng respondent sa impeachment trial na ito?

00:33:31.190 --> 00:33:38.700
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang ating pong vicepresidente, kasalukuyang ating pong subject sa ating continuing investigation, Mr.

00:33:46.780 --> 00:34:02.820
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Witness, may binanggit ka na continuing investigation ng NBI. Ano ang iyong ginawa kung mayroon man kaugnay ng ongoing investigation ng NBI na iyong binanggit?

00:34:07.730 --> 00:34:20.490
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa papamagitan ng pag-create po ng isang administrative order kung saan bumalangkas po tayo ng mga miyembro ng aming pong opisina para sila po ang mag-tuloy ng investigasyon na ito at mag-monitor po ng mga kailangan gawin.

00:34:21.920 --> 00:34:33.800
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Kaugnay pa rin ng binanggit mong Special Task Force. Ano ang kahalagahan nito sa investigasyon na ginagawa ng National Bureau of Investigation?

00:34:35.180 --> 00:34:54.340
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Napakahalaga po para sa amin sapagkat na from our law enforcement perspective ang ginawa pong banta ng vicepresidente ay tinatrato na naming hindi banta kundi isang plano para po sa pagpatay sa ating Pangulo and that is a threat to the President which we consider also na threat po sa ating national security.

00:34:56.080 --> 00:35:16.030
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Mr. Witness, anong katunayan mayroon ka kaugnay ng iyong binanggit na binuong Special Task Force upang mag-imbestiga sa lahat ng banta sa buhay ng Presidente, kasama na ang pagbabanta ng Vice Presidente?

00:35:16.040 --> 00:35:24.180
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Meron po akong in-issue na Administrative Order No. 11 noong April 16 ng kasalukuyang taon po.

00:35:25.840 --> 00:35:35.310
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: At kung ipapakita sa iyo ang kopya ng Administrative Order No. 11, ito ba ay makikilala mo?

00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:37.670
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Opo.

00:35:36.750 --> 00:36:01.240
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Honor, may we request that AO number 11, previously marked as Exhibit P429, be flushed. We likewise request, Your Honor, that Atty. Kyle Capunan, Assisting Counsel, be allowed to approach the witness. For confirmation of the document.

00:36:01.360 --> 00:36:23.040
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Assisting counsel for the prosecution may approach. And likewise, assisting counsel for the respondent may approach to confirm and validate the document being shown to the witness. Likewise, the text through the clerk of court is instructed to kindly flash in the screens the document being referred to by the lead prosecutor, the Honorable Luistro.

00:36:26.190 --> 00:36:27.850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly zoom it in, please.

