01:34:23.390 --> 01:34:24.230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 270.

01:34:26.260 --> 01:34:37.860
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: For purposes of submarking, Your Honor, may we ask which particular part of Paragraph 270 the witness first referred to?

01:34:38.200 --> 01:34:45.950
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, manifestation.

01:34:46.400 --> 01:34:48.240
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel for Respondent,

01:34:48.240 --> 01:35:11.530
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: may proceed. All right. Your Honor, this pertains to an affidavit of Arturo Lascañas, and on page 186, Your Honor, of such affidavit, it appears that even the signature is not a wet signature. It's a printed copy, and there's a subscription and sworn-to portion thereof, but it's not notarized at all. So this is a mere scrap of paper, Your Honor.

01:35:13.010 --> 01:35:44.550
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, the document is being presented only to seek confirmation from the witness that he is referring to this particular document as part of the investigation of Special Task Force. We are not presenting it to prove the truthfulness of the contents of the affidavit. The question only, Your Honor, is whether or not this is the document that was part of the consideration of the Special Task Force in investigating on the threat by the President to the life of the President.

01:35:44.560 --> 01:35:45.780
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: A short rejoinder, Your Honor.

01:35:45.960 --> 01:35:49.240
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel may give a rejoinder or additional manifestation.

01:35:49.500 --> 01:35:55.020
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Then we will not allow this witness to build on the basis of a mere scrap of paper, Your Honor.

01:35:56.100 --> 01:36:10.420
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel, it was the counsel for respondent who chose to use this copy instead of the one previously marked that I presume is either certified true

01:36:12.040 --> 01:36:15.960
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Or contains a more complete signature.

01:36:16.900 --> 01:36:43.080
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Then I would have to clarify, Your Honor, that it is our position. Well, first of all, we are not in the position to choose for this witness. But in the event that they use this document, we manifest, Your Honor, upon perusal that such document is unsigned and unnotarized, Your Honor. This is an affidavit. So, in other words, without the proper notarization and without the proper signature, then it's a mere scrap of paper. We cannot allow this witness to build his testimony based on

01:36:43.080 --> 01:36:43.840
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: this document.

01:36:44.360 --> 01:36:52.420
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: In fact, Your Honor, we request, Your Honor, that this court peruse also page 186 of such document.

01:36:53.000 --> 01:37:01.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before the court makes a ruling, the presiding officer makes a ruling, the pre-marked document, is it notarized?

01:37:02.410 --> 01:37:11.970
