01:40:03.690 --> 01:40:03.970
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: the court

01:40:03.970 --> 01:40:13.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: will allow it. Again, given the limited consideration that the court will give this testimony of the witness and not the truth of what he will read. Witness, may I answer?

01:40:15.070 --> 01:40:19.090
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Paragraph 270. The years of 2012 to 2013.

01:40:20.720 --> 01:40:39.860
Atty. Melvin Matibag: were the birth of Tokhang operations and the evil side of enforcement in Davao City by its author, the newly installed Davao City Police Office Director Colonel Ronald Bato de la Rosa. The operations were all cleared and approved by Mayors Inday Sara Zimmerman Duterte Carpio and Rodrigo Roa Duterte.

01:40:40.540 --> 01:40:47.860
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, we are requesting that the portion read by the witness be bracketed and marked as Exhibit P4-35.

01:40:51.660 --> 01:40:58.360
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: What else is the pertinent portion of this affidavit that you are referring to?

01:40:59.070 --> 01:41:03.130
Atty. Melvin Matibag: As mentioned earlier po, paragraph 270B.

01:41:04.280 --> 01:41:11.260
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: For the guidance of the Impeachment Court, kindly read for purposes of sub-marking only.

01:41:12.740 --> 01:42:07.450
Atty. Melvin Matibag: While eating, Colonel Bato de la Rosa told me in Visayan dialect why you summoned me and I quote, Tour, short of Arturo, my first name. Naka-historya mi ni Mayor Inday repairing to Davao City Mayor Inday Sara C. Duterte Carpio. Parti sa atwang tokhang operation. As part of our tokhang operation, ang order ni Mayor Inday sa akun nag-ilaylo sa nato ang pusil, killing through shooting sa atwang mga target persons. Shabu users and pushers and other criminal elements in Davao City. Kaysa mukhang siya media, magsige o paguntana, food, kidnapa, abdak, na lang ninyo ang inyong target o niya ilubong sa kwari, laud kwari, para missing lang kay okay si Mayor Inday saan

01:42:07.450 --> 01:42:41.310
Atty. Melvin Matibag: na paagi. I talked to Mary Inday as part of our Tokhang operation. She ordered us to laylaw our killings through gun shooting because the media is asking too much. Just kidnap targets, then bury them in the quarry so they would go missing. She is okay with that way. To which I answered, Yes, sir. Sultian na ko akwang grupo. I'll inform my group. Colonel Bato de la Rosa instructed me, I-inform tour kung naamoy ma-abduct ng target niyo. Inform me, tour, whenever you are kidnapped a target.

01:42:41.790 --> 01:42:50.290
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, we are requesting that that pertinent portion read by the witness be bracketed and marked as Exhibit P435A.

01:42:50.850 --> 01:42:53.510
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: So marked. It's ordered. Counsel for Respondent.

01:42:53.690 --> 01:42:53.950
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: What?

01:42:54.510 --> 01:43:07.510
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: We just want to register again our continuing objection, Your Honor. Again, we already allowed, Your Honor, that the witness at least identify this document.

01:43:09.420 --> 01:43:38.980
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: But as to the fact, Your Honor, that he is allowed to read even portions thereof, he is not the author of this affidavit. And as to the truth or falsity thereof, he is incompetent to testify on that. And it already violates the rights of our clients because she is being prejudiced. By the reading of this affidavit that cannot even be verified because the person is not here to testify. That's our objection, Your Honor.

01:43:39.100 --> 01:44:42.320
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Chair notes the objection and continuing objection of counsel for the respondent. And as an additional, for the third time perhaps, reminder of the Presiding Officer to my fellow Senator-Judges: the mention of statements allegedly made by then General Dela Rosa, now Senator Dela Rosa, are clearly hearsay even on the part of Lascañas himself. But as to the fact that probably he told him that, it may be established if the affidavit of Lascañas—and if Lascañas is presented here. Again, this is only as to the fact that this is what the NBI used in their investigation and coming up with their findings, not as to the truth of the statements being read by Director Matibag, much less the statements of other parties who did not execute this document. The continuing objection is noted. Witness may answer. Counsel will proceed.

01:44:44.610 --> 01:44:54.090
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: We are requesting your honor that that portion just read by the witness be bracketed and marked as P435A. Mr. Witness?

01:44:54.510 --> 01:44:55.430
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Let it be so, Mark.

01:44:55.690 --> 01:45:05.470
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Ano pa kung mayroon man? Ang mahalagang bahagi ng affidavit ni Arturo Lascañas na tinukoy mo kanina.

01:45:05.610 --> 01:45:07.030
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Same objection, your honors.

01:45:07.250 --> 01:45:08.650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Noted. Witness may answer.

01:45:08.950 --> 01:45:14.910
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa paragraph D po, 'yung portion po nito ay isa po sa aming pinagtuunan ng pansin sa aming imbestigasyon.

01:45:15.090 --> 01:45:17.550
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Please read for the purpose of sub-marking only.

01:45:20.400 --> 01:47:56.900
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I later called up retired senior police Sonny Buenaventura and relayed to him Colonel Ronald Bato de la Rosa's abduction operation ordered to me as allegedly ordered to him by Mayor Inday Sara Duterte Carpio. Sonny Buenaventura answered me that would personally confirm and verify the matter with Mayor Inday Duterte. Two days later, to my recollection, Sonny Buenaventura called me and instructed me to meet him in Caltex Gasoline Station parking area in front of SM Mall Ecoland. Matina, Davao City Mayor in Dysara, Duterte will meet him in the said place. Sonny Buenaventura wanted me to narrate personally to Mayor in Dysara about the abduction order of Colonel Ronald Bato de la Rosa regarding his Tokhang operation. I agreed. I immediately proceeded to Sonny Buenaventura's location. Upon my arrival on the board of my Strada pickup vehicle in Caltex Gasoline Station parking area, Sonny Buenaventura motioned me to board his pickup vehicle. However, before I could do so, Mayor Inday Sara Duterte Carpio arrived on board her SUV vehicle, a Fortuner-like vehicle, colored dark blue. Sonny Buenaventura then disembarked immediately from his vehicle and rushed to the vehicle of Mayor Inday Sara Duterte that stopped a few meters away from Sunny Bibintura's pickup vehicle. I stood in front of Sonny Buenaventura's pickup vehicle, looking and then talking. Mayor Inday Sara Duterte Carpio did not get up from the vehicle while talking to Sonny Buenaventura and Sonny was standing on the left side of Mayor Inday Sara Duterte vehicle. Then Sonny Buenaventura hand-signaled to me to come near him. I saw Mayor Inday Sara Z. Duterte Carpio inside her vehicle alone. I personally heard Mayor Inday Sara Zimmerman Duterte Carpio ordered Sonny Buenaventura and I in Bisayan dialect, and I quote, "Bulgar naman kayo man, pusilon (shoot) ang target ninyo "Nong" (referring to Sonny and myself, "Nong" short of Manong). Kidnapa na lang ninyo. (Target shabu users and pushers and other suspected criminal elements in Davao City) para missing lang para sila, para dili samok ang media." (Shooting your target is too brazen. Just kidnap them so they will just go missing and so that the media won't bother us).

01:47:57.380 --> 01:48:00.120
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sonny Buenaventura replied, "Sige, Day."

01:48:00.120 --> 01:48:30.310
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Okay. Then she drove away. It was a three-to-five-minute kill order through abduction operation from a lady mayor of our city, the daughter of Mayor President Rodrigo Roa Duterte, that shed much blood of [unclear] and poor Filipinos suspected of being shabu users and pushers in Davao City, now nationwide through the Tokhang campaign of the Philippine National Police, for four-star general and newly elected Senator Ronald ‘Bato’ de la Rosa.

01:48:30.310 --> 01:48:30.470
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor.

