03:35:50.780 --> 03:35:52.870
Atty. Melvin Matibag: At this point, Your Honor, not yet.

03:35:52.880 --> 03:35:54.670
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Not yet. Okay. Please proceed, counsel.

03:35:54.680 --> 03:35:57.190
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: That's enough. So no subpoena as of now.

03:35:58.570 --> 03:36:05.210
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: In other words, has there been any affidavit of investigation relating to contracting for assassination?

03:36:06.190 --> 03:36:15.270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: My understanding is there was a subpoena issued at that time during the investigation to the vice president and the lawyer submitted an affidavit.

03:36:15.390 --> 03:36:48.600
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Again, not responsive, Your Honor. I'm talking about an affidavit of investigation executed by the NBI. Not yet. So at this point, Would you agree with me that the DOJ has not found any basis for contracting for assassination? Wala pa po sa iyon. So at this point, as of today, there is simply no evidence to warrant the filing of a formal charge for contracting for assassination, correct?

03:36:48.860 --> 03:36:59.200
Atty. Melvin Matibag: That's why, kung babalikan po natin yung aking testimonya, this is a continuing and an open investigation as to the contracting of a killer.

03:36:59.200 --> 03:37:05.800
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: in other words, the reason why these are not present at this time because your investigation is still ongoing. It's

03:37:05.800 --> 03:37:08.120
Atty. Melvin Matibag: a case build up and an open active investigation.

03:37:08.380 --> 03:37:53.790
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Very well. Now, you mentioned about grave threats and inciting to sedition. My question to you is, these subject matters fall under the category of felonies, correct? That's correct. Now, in fact, Based on the penalties involved as provided by law, these fall under the jurisdiction of the first-level trial courts, correct? Yes. Moreover, for one to be declared guilty of these felonies, the burden of proof is guilt beyond reasonable doubt, correct? That is correct. Now, guilt beyond reasonable doubt, is this a low threshold or a high threshold?

03:37:55.210 --> 03:37:57.670
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Beyond reasonable doubt, of course, it's a high threshold.

03:37:57.930 --> 03:38:11.340
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: In fact, it is the highest threshold in criminal law, correct? So in other words, para lang for the benefit of the Filipino people watching, so hindi ka pwedeng magsampa ng kaso ng hindi mo kayang patunayan, correct?

03:38:11.810 --> 03:38:22.770
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po yan. Dahil meron pong Memorandum Circular No. 20 ng Department of Justice kung saan sinasabi that when you file cases, there should be a reasonable certainty of conviction.

03:38:23.170 --> 03:38:46.030
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you for that clarification. So, if this threshold of guilt beyond reasonable doubt is not reached, then the accused must be acquitted, correct? Tama po yan. And in so far as grave threats or inciting to sedition, it is the trial courts that will decide that, correct? That is correct. Not the DOJ?

03:38:46.270 --> 03:38:56.270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: The DOJ will submit the information and the resolution for prosecution at the end of the day. It will be the court who will say whether it's guilty or not.

03:38:57.420 --> 03:39:36.810
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Now, in your testimony earlier, you mentioned that there are leads. On the alleged person that VP Sara talked to, correct? Yes. But let me ask you this. During that presscon, did VP Sara mention the word assassin? Wala po. Alright. Now, the investigation on these leads, are these already final? Pakiulit po. The investigation based on these leads that you mentioned, are these already final? Hindi po.

03:39:37.070 --> 03:39:40.990
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Walinaw po sinabi ko that this is a continuing and open investigation po.

03:39:41.090 --> 03:39:57.530
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. So, in other words, you haven't given any opportunity for VP Sara to confront this alleged person, correct? Hindi po po. Alright. But, will you agree with me that confronting this alleged person is part of due process?

03:39:58.180 --> 03:40:04.720
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po. Kaya mas maganda nga po kung si VP Sara mismo magsabi dito kung meron siyang kinausap at kung sino ang kinausap.

03:40:06.820 --> 03:40:12.980
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: But is that part of the SOP also that you give an opportunity for VP Sara to confront?

03:40:13.300 --> 03:40:26.640
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po. Pag natukoy na po namin kung sino ang taong kanyang kinausap, that is the time na siya po yamin kukomprontahin para siya po ay masagot niya kung itong taong talaga ito ang kanyang kinausap para patayin ang Pangulo.

03:40:26.760 --> 03:40:40.270
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. My next question is very simple. So you offered your testimony before this Impeachment Court. Even you performed SOP or giving opportunity to VP Sara to confront?

03:40:40.870 --> 03:40:58.150
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Malinaw naman po yung sinabi ko. Pag nakita po namin kung sino ang taong kinausap, saka po namin siya kukomprontahin kasama po ang taong iyon at kasama po ang mga willing na nagbibigay ng UNINTEL para harapin po. Ang kusasyon na iyon. So

03:40:58.150 --> 03:41:04.830
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: considering that you're still pursuing those leads, don't you think that your testimony today is premature? Hindi po.

03:41:05.050 --> 03:41:39.810
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sapagkat malinaw naman po sa statement ng ating vicepresidente na meron siyang kinausap para patayin si Bongbong Marcos, si Lisa Marcos Araneta, si Martin Romualdez, at sinabi pa niya na walang biro to us sa law investigation. Applying po namin. Ang mga metodology na ginagamit ng Secret Service sa Amerika ay papasok po rito na ito ay isang malinaw na confession ng isang tao na meron siyang isang plano na pagpatay. Okay,

03:41:39.870 --> 03:41:50.050
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: I'll move on. But I'll ask you, isn't that a trial by publicity which is not sanctioned by your laws? Hindi

03:41:50.050 --> 03:42:22.080
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Hindi po. Sapagkat kaya nga po namin hindi nilalabas yung aming confidential at secret na investigation, lamang nga po tayo'y pinatitestigo rito na kailangan natin sabihin kung ano na ang naging takbo ng investigation. At malinaw naman po sa aking testimonya na dito sa continuing open investigation, active investigation, meron pong mga persons of interest.

03:42:22.080 --> 03:42:41.680
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: fact, you mentioned during your direct testimony that you cannot give further details, correct? It's classified. Okay. So, with all due respect, I'll ask this in Filipino, with all due respect to you, Director Matibag, kung hindi niyo pa po pala kayang magbigay ng detalye, bakit niyo pa po nilabas na may leads kayo in the first place?

03:42:42.340 --> 03:43:00.380
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa pagkat gaya po nang sinabi ko, malinaw naman na yung pagsasalita ng ating vicepresidente na siya ay kumausap ng papatay at pumayag yung papatay na patayin ang mga individual na ito, meron na pong pagkakasundo na gagawin po ang isang krimen.

03:43:00.680 --> 03:43:09.840
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Yeah, but my point is, wouldn't that prejudice your ongoing investigation, that you come out here and you make statements that you already have leads?

03:43:10.320 --> 03:43:12.240
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Objection, Your Honor. That is a speculative.

03:43:14.740 --> 03:43:15.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Witness may answer.

03:43:17.120 --> 03:43:26.420
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Kaya nga po ang dahilan na hindi ko mabanggit kung sino po 'yung mga persons of interest, dahil doon po mako-compromise ang imbestigasyon na gumugulong.

03:43:26.480 --> 03:43:43.200
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. At any rate, if this ongoing investigation progresses, that is the only time that a different charge will be executed against the Vice President.

03:43:43.360 --> 03:44:07.860
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Balikan ko po ulit. Para po sa amin, malinaw na ang pagkontrata sa pagpapatay o nang papatay sa mga pangalang binanggit ay nandoon na, applying the methodology ng Secret Service na binanggit ko po kanina. Ang hindi na lang po natin nakikita ay kung sino ang taong kinausap. Kaya ito po ay still open and continuing investigation.

03:44:08.170 --> 03:44:25.070
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: At any rate, it's not yet final, correct? Tama po. Now, you mentioned that the NBI is still conducting an investigation, ongoing investigation. Do you still use the video of the November 23, 2024 presscon in this ongoing investigation?

03:44:25.590 --> 03:44:33.660
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Isa po ito sabi naging batayan. Para po dun sa five-point standard na pinitingnan po namin ay amin pong matugunan.

03:44:34.100 --> 03:44:39.300
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: It's an almost two-year-old video now. Do you think it's still relevant to your ongoing investigation?

03:44:39.920 --> 03:44:46.520
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Hindi po. Sa pagkatagang sa ngayon nga ay hindi pa natin naahanap kung sino ang taong kinausap po ng ating vice president.

03:44:46.640 --> 03:45:21.590
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Very well. Atty. Matibag, do you know Mel Sabio? Opo. Now, about two months ago, An old audio video file of the two of you circulated online. By the way, we won't show that video out of respect to the party's rights as well as I saw your wife here also out of your family member's rights and also out of Mel Sabio's rights. I'll just ask you a few questions. This video circulated online and you already came out in the media admitting that it was you and Mel Sabio who were involved in that video.

03:45:22.110 --> 03:45:26.690
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po yun. That is a private conversation sa dalawa pong magkaibigan na hindi nagkakasundo.

03:45:27.290 --> 03:45:35.960
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. And my only question to you is this. Did that incident demonstrate an emotional outburst on your part?

03:45:36.640 --> 03:45:48.600
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Kasama na po yun. Kombinasyon na ng galit at disappointment. At ako naman po inamin ko na yan ay isang pagkakamali na akin pong tinanggap na rin at tinagsisiyan.

03:45:48.780 --> 03:45:51.560
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. Could you recall what you said in that video?

03:45:52.020 --> 03:45:57.560
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang masama po yung aking mga sinabi. Meron pong hindi talaga kaaya-aya. Can

03:45:57.560 --> 03:46:01.460
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: you recall? Just to give an idea of those who are not able to watch.

03:46:01.480 --> 03:46:06.020
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I cannot exactly recall because that was really long time ago. That's

03:46:06.020 --> 03:46:06.180
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: okay.

03:46:07.830 --> 03:46:15.540
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Now, on July 10, 2026, you wrote a letter to Representative Luistro. Do you confirm this?

03:46:17.180 --> 03:47:03.710
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: July 10? July 10, 2026. Opo. In that letter, we can confront you with a hard copy, but we can also flash. In that letter, you mentioned, and I quote, As Director of the Bureau, I will personally attend to represent the NBI at this summit of Director and Commissioner General level law enforcement leaders across the Asia Pacific. Which will require my travel and attendance on those dates. Now, those dates pertain to July 21 to 22, 2026. So, today and tomorrow. Do you confirm this? Opo. Alright. Now, in that letter,

03:47:05.610 --> 03:47:18.550
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: there was a prior letter to that, correct? Which you received from FBI Director Kash Patel? Tama po. Do you personally know Kash Patel? G.

03:47:21.640 --> 03:47:25.950
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Matibag, Atty.

03:47:38.480 --> 03:47:42.430
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Matibag, Atty.

03:47:45.160 --> 03:48:01.700
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Through the prosecution on July 13, 2026. Now, just a manifestation, this now forms part of the records of this case. So, are you friends or did he just research about your being a lawyer? Ganito po kasi ang

03:48:01.440 --> 03:49:23.350
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ganito po kasi ang nangyari diyan. Meron pong high-value target, one of the top ten most wanted, si Henry Kimball ang pangalan po niya, who scammed the government about 2.8 billion. Number two po siya at sa 10 most wanted. And we had a coordination meeting with our local counterpart ng U.S. Embassy na FBI station in Manila, si Ma'am Courtney, asking for our help for the extradition of this person who happens to have a problem in a court in Makati. They were expecting na ito pong taong ito ay matagal pa bago ma-extradite sa kanila. Lumapit po sa atin sa NBI, at dahil natulungan po natin na yung inaakala nilang buwan ang lilipas bago ma-extradite, natulungan po natin sila sa loob ng dalawang araw ay na-extradite po. Kung kaya nung na-extradite po ito pong si Henry Kimball, ako po ay tinawagan ni Ma'am Courtney ng FBI na siya'y nasa America at sinabi na nagpapasalamat. Katunayan po, nagpadala po ng letter of gratitude ang FBI. At yun pong pag-attend ko sa Bangkok, hindi naman po basta lang ako a-attend doon sa conference. There was an opportunity on the side na magkaroon po kami ng pagpupulong po nang personal ni Director Kash Patel. Kaya po gusto ko sanang makadalo doon.

03:49:23.360 --> 03:49:46.750
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Thank you for that clarification. Anyway, I'm just asking because the schedule of the court actually changed or was altered because of this letter. Just a few questions on this. Now, upon perusal of this letter, it appears na sinulatan kayo nang diretso ni Director Kash Patel, and walang address yung NBI. It just says Manila. Do you confirm receipt of this letter?

03:49:46.760 --> 03:49:48.030
Atty. Melvin Matibag: It was sent through email.

03:49:48.040 --> 03:49:59.640
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Through email. Okay. Now, of course, before you wrote Representative Luistro, you first confirmed your attendance with FBI Director Patel. Am I right?

03:49:59.650 --> 03:50:46.830
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala pa pong confirmation, dahil malinaw naman po. Sinasabi ko nga po kay Congresswoman Luistro na dalawang event 'yan na magkasabay. Sayang yung opportunity na maaari kong makausap yung FBI Director, sapagkat it's very rare that an FBI Director will talk to an NBI Director. So sinabi ko na baka naman puwedeng mas mapaaga, kung puwede lang, at kung makikita naman po doon sa liham ko, respectfully I'm requesting. Pero nilinaw ko po kay Congresswoman Luistro na dalawang event 'yan, at in order of priority, ang akin pong priority ay tumestigo po dito po sa Impeachment Court. At sabi ko naman, ipinaabot ko po through Ma'am Courtney that probably we can arrange another day na magkausap po kami ni Director Kash Patel.

03:50:46.840 --> 03:50:56.190
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. Thank you for that clarification. At any rate, you're admitting that before you wrote Representative Luistro, hindi pa final yung confirmation mo dito kay Director?

03:50:56.200 --> 03:51:06.230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Meron na pong arrangement. Pero alam po nila na ako'y magtitistigo. So kung malilipat po, that is the only time na ako po ay pupunta sa Bangkok po.

03:51:06.240 --> 03:51:12.390
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: No, I'm talking about: may confirmation na kayo ni Director Kash Patel before you wrote Representative Luistro?

03:51:12.400 --> 03:51:19.190
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala pa. There was already an invitation and information channeled to their local representative, si Ma'am Courtney po.

03:51:19.720 --> 03:51:20.710
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Ma'am, sino 'yan, ma'am?

03:51:20.720 --> 03:51:23.270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Siya po si Courtney. Siya po yung FBI representative dito.

03:51:23.720 --> 03:51:33.270
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: At any rate, my question is: do you maintain that this is an official invitation from FBI, Kash Patel?

03:51:33.280 --> 03:51:38.350
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Opo. Katunayan, meron pong dumalo ngayon doon, yung pong aming representative ng IOD.

03:51:38.360 --> 03:51:42.070
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: And it's also director or commissioner level?

03:51:42.080 --> 03:51:44.990
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ah, ano po, siya po ay division level po.

03:51:45.000 --> 03:51:47.230
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Are you at liberty to disclose the name?

03:51:47.240 --> 03:51:48.910
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes po, Atty. Chris Hernandez.

03:51:48.920 --> 03:51:50.750
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Nandun siya sa Bangkok ngayon. Nandun po siya ngayon.

03:51:50.760 --> 03:51:55.630
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Would you know kung si Director Kash Patel nag-attend doon sa Bangkok ngayon or nag-cancel din siya?

03:51:55.640 --> 03:51:57.630
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Hindi ko po alam. I have to get the information.

03:51:58.670 --> 03:52:22.410
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Just one last manifestation, Your Honor. Again, these documents comprising of three documents, June 24, July 10, and July 13, were introduced by the prosecution and are now part of the records of this case. If I may be allowed to proceed, Your Honor. Now, I'll show you one last graphic and then I'll ask you a couple of questions thereafter.

03:52:24.030 --> 03:52:27.530
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Can we show the graphic? Alright.

03:52:31.070 --> 03:52:35.110
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: This is from the Daily Tribune. Your

03:52:35.110 --> 03:52:36.430
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Honor, please. No

03:52:36.430 --> 03:52:38.470
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: question yet, Your Honor. Let

03:52:38.470 --> 03:52:43.230
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: counsel finish with this question and then the lead prosecutor may make her objection.

03:52:43.770 --> 03:53:25.210
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. This is from the Daily Tribune. Okay. And this is the public, entitled public trust rating. I'll just focus on the green. Not the red. No, but Vice President Sarah Duterte, it says they're 57%. And this was conducted by the Social Weather Station's SWS survey. Okay. Now, my question to you is this. You mentioned that you have an ongoing investigation. Do materials like this, insofar as how Filipino people view or trust VP Sara, Have an effect in your investigation.

03:53:25.570 --> 03:53:30.410
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Objection, Your Honor. Before the witness answers, the lead prosecutor is recognized for objection. What is the basis of the objection?

03:53:30.810 --> 03:53:46.530
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, the defense is showing a picture of the president and the vice president with a certain rating at the bottom. This has no relevance at all, Your Honor. With respect to the subject matter of this impeachment trial,

03:53:46.830 --> 03:53:47.650
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: and we

03:53:47.650 --> 03:53:50.910
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: are objecting to the presentation of this picture, Your Honor.

03:53:51.090 --> 03:53:53.350
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Just a short rejoinder, Your Honor.

03:53:53.810 --> 03:53:59.570
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: The witness

03:53:59.570 --> 03:54:12.890
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: mentioned the term betrayal of public trust, and we can run the TSN back. Your Honor, of course, we're allowed, this is cross-examination, we're allowed to present controverting evidence to that statement.

03:54:14.360 --> 03:54:26.780
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The Chair will allow the witness to answer despite that there is no date when this survey was taken. Kindly answer if you know, Director Matibag.

03:54:26.940 --> 03:55:08.390
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Gladly, Mr. Presiding Officer. Alam ninyo po, survey iyan. And all of us know, or for the information of the public, a survey is just a snapshot of something. It doesn't necessarily follow na yung survey na iyan ay kumbaga nakataga na sa bato. Pangalawa po, may mandato po ang NBI. We cannot be swayed by public opinion o kaya po ng aming personal na opinyon. Kami po ay nag-iimbestiga na batay sa batas, batay sa proseso, at batay po sa ating itinakdang mandato base po sa pagtatatag ng NBI.

03:55:11.560 --> 03:55:25.420
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. I mentioned Daily Tribune. You write editorials for the Daily Tribune, correct? Tama po. Long time ago po. Long time ago. And in 2024, you wrote at least three editorials about VP Sara. Is that... Can you recall?

03:55:26.280 --> 03:55:29.420
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Mari po. Mayroon po akong mga sinulat tungkol kay Vice President.

03:55:29.520 --> 03:55:57.120
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: I'm showing you this... No, not that one. The editorials, alright, from the Daily Tribune. And we have hard copies that you can refer to. But it says here, Director Belvin Matibag, do you confirm that it is you who authored these editorials? Yes. Alright. Now, I'm showing you the first one entitled, Inday Sara, The Bratinella, dated September 12, 2024. Do you confirm that you wrote this editorial?

03:55:57.740 --> 03:55:59.700
Atty. Melvin Matibag: That's correct, in my opinion column.

03:56:00.000 --> 03:56:27.550
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright. And you also wrote... The Bratinella is a flat spare tire. Dated October 24, 2024. Do you confirm this? Yes. And you also wrote, Bratinella, Sarah, and her bad habits dated November 7, 2024. Do you confirm this? Yes. And in these editorials, you shared your opinions against VP Sarah. Is that correct?

03:56:27.910 --> 03:56:42.240
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, unang-una po. Siguro doon sa title na Bratinella, that is not my original. In fact, kaya ako po nasulat dyan, eh yan ang mismong naririnig ko nang kami magkakasama nila dating Pangulong Duterte na ang tawag niya kay Inday Saha ay Bratinella.

03:56:42.660 --> 03:56:52.340
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, so my only question is before you testified today, there were already instances in the past that you shared your public opinions against VP Sala.

03:56:52.440 --> 03:56:57.110
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, that is a opinion column. At meron po tayong mga pinagbabasihan dyan.

03:56:57.230 --> 03:57:37.450
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Okay. In fact, let me read one line from your editorial. It says there, As Inday Sara is being unmasked in the legislative inquiries and by her own mouth, as an ill-bred Bratinella, her public trust crumbles. Do you confirm that you included this statement in your editorial? Yan po yung nakasulat. Alright. And despite this position, And the recent surveys show that VP Sara even gained positive trust rating as shown earlier, a positive 57. Do you confirm this?

03:57:37.890 --> 03:57:43.570
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, again, I'm saying na nung sinulat ko po yan, that is my opinion as an opinion writer. Alright.

03:57:43.790 --> 03:57:51.050
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Now, despite this positive trust rating by VP Sara, do you still maintain that, and I quote, her public trust crumbles?

03:57:52.040 --> 03:58:11.210
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, Para sa akin po na ako yung NBI Director, palagi ko po hindi po material itong ating pinag-uusapan sapagkat sabi ko nga ang ating pag-iimbestigay nababasis sa batas, nababasis sa ebidensya, at prosesong nanduduna nang ako'y dumating po bilang NBI Director.

03:58:11.690 --> 03:58:23.380
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Alright, one last question on this before I let this point go. So considering the positive trust rating of VP Sara, can one really say that she betrayed public trust? Magkaiba

03:58:23.380 --> 03:58:24.540
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: po yan. It's speculative, Your Honor.

03:58:25.380 --> 03:58:31.480
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Can we get a ruling, Your Honor? Witness is knowledgeable enough to answer. He can handle himself. Director Matibag, you may answer.

03:58:32.140 --> 03:58:59.870
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Magkaiba po yan. Again, I'm saying, and I'm sure marami rin po rito nakakaalam na umaasa sa mga survey, a survey is just a snapshot of what's happening. It doesn't necessarily follow na pagka yun ang lumabas, ay yun na yung totoo. Pangalwa. Pagka po ating pinagbasihan ng popularidad, ang ibig sabihin po ba nito ang isang pinakakilala at popular na tao pwede nang gumawa ng krimen at hindi natin papapanagutin?

03:59:21.130 --> 04:00:25.260
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: It is the right of the respondent to intelligently cross-examine him on those topics. Again, Your Honor, those topics are not included in the Articles of Impeachment and are considered new. In fact, Your Honor, as earlier stated, we feel that these two topics are a violation of the respondent's right to be promptly and fully informed of the charges against her. As a result of the cross-examination, a 100-page document was introduced and allowed by this court. That document is unsigned and unnotarized. We feel like, for us to intelligently cross-examine the witness on this document that he mentioned, there is a need for a continuance, Your Honor.

04:00:25.780 --> 04:00:27.520
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: What does the lead prosecutor say?

04:00:28.260 --> 04:01:18.860
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: With all due respect, Your Honor, we object to the motion for continuance of the defense. The defense already started and propounded a lot of cross-examination questions to the witness, and the witness is simply answering completely, accurately, the questions which are being raised and propounded to him. We do not understand, Your Honor, why they will move for continuance after already raising a lot of questions to the witness, Your Honor. We would like, Your Honor, the defense to finish. The cross-examination today and if the impeachment court will still allow, we will immediately proceed to redirect after the cross-examination, Your Honor, with all due respect to our honorable senator judges.

04:01:19.120 --> 04:02:07.780
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The objection of the lead prosecutor is noted. However, this is the first time that any counsel for the parties is asking for a continuance. The chair is inclined to grant it and will so grant it as well. Should the council for the prosecutors or the lead prosecutor or panel of prosecutors require it at some point in time in this trial or hearing, but let it not be the rule or let it not be a habit on the part of either council for the parties to do so, to ask for a continuance. But at this time, the chair will grant the continuance requested by the defense. In the meantime, since it's only 5.55 with the indulgence of our senator judges, We may proceed to the interjections and interventions of the Senator Judges.

04:02:08.420 --> 04:02:11.100
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: One last point, Your Honor, before the interjections.

04:02:11.320 --> 04:02:17.900
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before recognizing the Senator Judges, yes, what is the pleasure of Atty. Vinlon?

04:02:18.060 --> 04:02:27.370
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, considering that the witness introduced... As I said, a lengthy document. Can we ask for a copy of the Las Cañas material that he provided? The

04:02:27.370 --> 04:02:49.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: chair already earlier ordered that, I believe. During the interregnum, the prosecutors are directed to kindly furnish the council for respondents with a copy of the, I believe, over an inch or a little less than two inches of affidavit of Mr. Las Cañas. So ordered.

04:02:53.510 --> 04:03:12.810
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Chair will now recognize. Prior to Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo earlier, Senator Judge Villanueva indicated his desire to interject or make interventions. Thereafter, Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo. Thereafter, Senator Judge Risa Ontiveros. You have two minutes, sir, and you may proceed when you're ready.

04:03:16.000 --> 04:04:46.980
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Mr. Presiding Officer, before I ask some questions, I can see that my time is already running. Let me just ask a procedural inquiry Mr. Presiding Officer and respectfully this representation seek the guidance of the court on a procedural matter because earlier today I heard our witness who made mention several times that the investigation is still ongoing It's a continuing investigation. May we know, Mr. Presiding Officer, in this particular aspect of the NBI's investigation that remains ongoing, Just for the guidance of this representation and I'm sure for the guidance of both parties, kung matatapos na po yung investigation o yung presentation of evidence dito po sa Article 4 at magkakaroon po ng significant development na maaari pong material sa atin pong proceedings, ano po ang tamang proseso para maipabatid At kung kinakailangan maiharap po ito sa Impeachment Court considering na isasara na po itong Presentation of Evidence sa Article 4, State

04:04:46.980 --> 04:05:20.340
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: History. Sen. Judge Villanueva, sa rule, the Court is a passive body. Hindi pang ihimasukan ng husgado kung ano man ang pwede, balak o gustong gawin ng magkabilang partido, prosecution man o sa hanay ng respondent kung mangyari man yun. And the court will not speculate with respect to that hypothetical situation should it arise lest we be accused of prejudging or deciding certain matters for the parties that they should be the one deciding should that happen.

04:05:20.600 --> 04:06:07.340
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you very much, Mr. President—Mr. Presiding Officer. And in fact, I would suggest: ‘May, motu proprio or upon motion, with hearing in either case, reopen the proceedings to avoid a miscarriage of justice.’ Close quote. So, just to put on record, Mr. Presiding Officer, na ito po yung magiging proper procedure. Marami pong salamat.

04:06:07.460 --> 04:06:27.700
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: That is an option that the court may take, as the rule itself suggests. But at this juncture, the Presiding Officer would rather leave it to the parties, given that this is an adversarial proceeding. And the party should know what they should do for the interest of their respective clients. You may proceed, sir, with your questions. You have two minutes.

04:06:27.800 --> 04:07:10.740
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Thank you, Mr. President. Just one question to our witness, Director Matibag, for the benefit of the court and this representation. Mahari po ba ninyong ipaliwanag kung paano... Inaevaluate po ng National Bureau of Investigation ang isang aligasyon na ang isang tao ay nag-utos o kumontrata ng iba upang magsagawa ng isang krimen. Bilang bahagi po ng inyong investigasyon, tinukoy po ba ninyo kung ang ganito pong aligasyon ay maaaring pumasok?

04:07:19.300 --> 04:07:21.920
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Director Matibag, I'd like to ask this question

04:07:40.930 --> 04:08:02.650
Sen. Joel Villanueva: PINAL LAWS Now, the constitutional function of this court, however, is different. We are not sitting as a criminal court to determine guilt beyond reasonable doubt. Rather, we are called upon to determine whether the respondent's alleged acts constitute impeachable offenses.

04:08:05.770 --> 04:08:36.490
Sen. Joel Villanueva: So magkaiba po yung binabanggit natin na criminal liability at constitutional accountability. Hindi po lahat ng maaaring maging batayan ng impeachment ay kailangan tumutumbas sa isang krimen. Sa pagkat ang impeachment ay hindi naman po usapin lamang ng paglabag sa batas kung hindi paglabag sa tiwalang ipinagkakaloob ng taong bayan. Ano pong masasabi nyo dito, Mr. Witness?

04:08:36.990 --> 04:09:57.750
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Your Honor, tama po yun. Doon po sa uling sinabi ninyo na hindi naman nangangahulugan kung may krimi na nangyari, ito ay impeachable offense. Pero ilagay po natin sa pangyayaring to, kaya naman po, yung pong investigasyon doon sa grave threat, At doon po sa exciting to sedition, malinaw po ito na napapaloob sa revised penal code. At yun naman po pag-iimbestiga at paghahanap doon sa taong kinausap para pumatay, hindi po ito napapaloob sa revised penal code dahil yung pagpaplano ng pagpatay ay hindi naman po pinaparusahan yan kung hindi nga nagawa. Subalit doon na po papasok yung sinasabi nga natin na meron pong sinasabi na sa impeachment tinitingnan po at para sa akin nga yung betrayal of public trust. Dito po po pasok. Bakit po? Dahil meron po siyang sinumpang tungkulin. Doon po mismo sa kanyang out of office bilang vice president. Sinabi niya that protect and defend the constitution, execute the laws, do justice to everyone, and consecrate herself to protect the nation. Pero doon po siya sinabing execute the laws. Dito po natin nakikita hindi po execute the laws, yung pag-usap ng papatay. That is to execute the President. Kaya doon po papasok yung magkaiba na BTL or Public Trust.

04:09:59.680 --> 04:10:13.600
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Naiintindihan ko po yung binabanggit ninyo: yung role ninyo na limitado doon sa criminal investigation at yung findings po ninyo. Hindi po ibig sabihin ay impeachable offense kaagad-agad.

04:10:13.600 --> 04:10:14.390
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

04:10:14.400 --> 04:11:03.150
Sen. Joel Villanueva: And again, that's why I'm putting into the records na this is not a criminal proceeding but an impeachment proceeding. Last but not the least, doon sa binanggit po ninyo, there is a difference between saying that an individual has not yet been identified and saying also that no such individual exists. So ang una, nangangahulugan na nagpapatuloy pa po yung bureau sa pag-verify at pag-validate ng impormasyong mayroon ito. Sa ikalawa naman po ay isang konklusyon matapos ang isang imbestigasyon. Director Matibag, maaari po ba ninyong ipaliwanag yung kahalagahan ng distinction na ito sa point of view of the NBI sa inyong pag-iimbestiga?

04:11:02.750 --> 04:11:05.530
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Doon na po natin hinihiwalay.

04:11:05.550 --> 04:11:12.750
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before the witness answers, kindly wind up after that question, Senator Judge Joel. Witness may answer.

04:11:13.030 --> 04:11:23.470
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Doon nga po natin hinihiwalay yung investigasyon na nangyari doon sa grief threat at inciting to sedition. Pumasok na po tayo doon sa pag-iimbestiga.

04:11:35.290 --> 04:11:47.490
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang naging basihan nga po dito yung aking testimonya kanina na yung five-point field po na pinagbabasihan ng National Threat Assessment Center na ginagamit po ng Secret Service po ng Amerika.

04:11:48.290 --> 04:12:05.750
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Okay po. Siguro hilingin ko na lang, Mr. Presiding Officer, at sa ating witness, kung matapos po yung inyong ongoing at sinasabi niyo nga po ang continue investigation, ay ma-inform lang din po ang courting ito. Maraming salamat, Your Honors, Mr. Presiding Officer.

04:12:05.750 --> 04:12:17.050
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Villanueva. Senator Judge Tulfo Raffi is recognized for his interjections and interventions. You have two minutes, sir, for your questions. You may proceed when you're ready.

04:12:20.720 --> 04:12:25.840
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Mr. Witness, are you familiar with the case of Ronell Mas?

04:12:27.030 --> 04:12:29.570
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Opo, napanood ko po 'yan.

04:12:29.610 --> 04:12:37.810
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: At that time, hindi pa kayong NBI Director or connected to the NBI whatsoever. So, tell us briefly dito sa kaso ni Ronell Mas.

04:12:38.030 --> 04:12:41.590
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa pagkaalala ko po rito, itong si Ronell Mas ay isang guro

04:12:41.590 --> 04:12:42.430
Atty. Melvin Matibag: na

04:12:42.430 --> 04:13:12.770
Atty. Melvin Matibag: kung saan siya ay nagsabi na kung sino ang papatay sa dating Pangulong. Rodrigo Ruo D. Torti, Atty. E papabiwaan niya ng 50 million. At sa pagkakaalala ko po, ang National Bureau of Investigation rin po ang tumugis at tumuli sa kanya, particularly po ang aming pong opisina sa Region 1. At siya po ay kinusuhan po ng pagbabanta at itinuring po na ang threat niya ay isang malaking threat po. Hindi lamang sa dating Pangulo kundi po sa ating pong National Security.

04:13:18.990 --> 04:13:25.890
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Inciting to sedition. And he was arrested warrantless. It was a warrantless arrest, right?

04:13:26.070 --> 04:13:26.610
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

04:13:28.180 --> 04:13:48.350
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. So, isang guro nagbanta sa dating Pangulo, agad-agad inaresto ng walang warat. Now, itong si, yung VP Sara, si Vice President Sara Duterte, na nagbanta rin kay Pangulong Duterte at kay Pangulong Marcos. Anong difference ng dalawang?

04:13:49.030 --> 04:14:05.990
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, ang pagkakaiba po nila, itong si Rene Mas ay isang guro, si vice president ay isa namang pong vice president, at siguro po ito ang naging konsiderasyon kung bakit hindi siya inaresto agad. So ibig sabihin ng NBI pala ay

04:14:05.990 --> 04:14:10.590
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: tumitingin sa tinatawag ng special treatment. So ibig sabihin hindi pala pata sa NBI.

04:14:16.220 --> 04:14:31.880
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I cannot speak

04:14:31.950 --> 04:15:11.970
Atty. Melvin Matibag: for the NBA at that time, Your Honor, sapagkat yung mga pangyayari pong iyan, wala naman ako sa NBA pa po. Subalit ang maaaring ko pong ibahagi sa inyo, ipamarapatin po ninyo, ayun na nga pong aking pakikipagtalastasan sa aming mga foreign counterparts na aking din napag-aralan at sinasabi nila na sa kanilang jurisdiction kung mayroong isang pagbabanta na ginawa ng vicepresidente ay maaaring agad na ikulong at matanggal ka agad po sa pwesto. Pero again, respectfully, I cannot speak for the NBI noon po at saka yung Pagyayari po doon po.

04:15:12.050 --> 04:15:28.150
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Ano ibig sabihin po ni para sa inyo, Mayor Baste, nung sinabi niya sa isang Rage Coalition Gathering, isang ulo lang naman ang kailangan namin at ang ulo ni BBM or Bongbong Marcos. What does it mean to you?

04:15:28.330 --> 04:15:38.350
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, kagaya po na nga aking naging testimonya, itirinato po namin ito na isang threat sa isang banta sa ating Pangulo na transcends all situa threat to our national security.

04:15:39.050 --> 04:15:49.260
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So is it the same as saying may patong sa ulo ang isang tao like a reward whoever can capture this person dead or alive or something to that effect?

04:15:50.000 --> 04:16:01.100
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Itinuturing po namin itong banta hindi lamang sa siguridad ng ating Pangulo kundi sa siguridad po ng ating bansa.

04:16:01.100 --> 04:16:08.730
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So again kung tinuturing yung threat itong salita na binitiwan ni Bastet or Mayor Bastet Duterte

04:16:10.400 --> 04:16:11.040
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Atty.

04:16:19.270 --> 04:16:21.550
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Ronell M. Mas, Atty. Duterte,

04:16:21.550 --> 04:16:22.770
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Atty.

04:16:30.750 --> 04:16:32.070
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ronell M. So,

04:16:34.250 --> 04:16:36.130
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: why was he not arrested?

04:16:40.460 --> 04:16:41.360
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Atty. Ronell Mas.

04:16:42.280 --> 04:17:04.780
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Dahil naging warrantless arrest, siya po ay na-dismiss ang kaso. So iyan din po yung iniingatan natin.

04:17:04.780 --> 04:17:05.260
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: you, Mr. Witness.

04:17:06.020 --> 04:17:13.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo. Senator Judge Rison Tiveros is recognized. You may proceed, ma'am, when you're ready and you have two minutes.

04:17:15.720 --> 04:17:31.580
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer. Mr. Witness, nung nakaraang hearing po, paulit-ulit na binabanggit ang pangalan ni Princess Maui. Sino po ba yung taong yan? Background po niya, profile po niya?

04:17:31.800 --> 04:17:34.740
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa pagkakalam ko, isa po siyang vlogger.

04:17:36.760 --> 04:17:40.160
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Ano pong background niya? Paano siya naging vlogger?

04:17:40.500 --> 04:17:54.820
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Iyan po yung tinatawag natin. At alam naman ng lahat na DDS po. I see.

04:17:54.820 --> 04:18:05.840
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: ano po yung bukod doon na vlogger siya doon sa panig na iyon, meron pa bang ibang profile itong Princess Maui bilang vlogger?

04:18:06.700 --> 04:18:21.260
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Katunayan po, I was informed that she or he was invited to the NBI pero hindi po siya dumalok. At yan po ay kasama rin po sa patuloy na sinusubaybayan po ng ating cybercrime division po.

04:18:21.440 --> 04:18:49.170
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Alright, salamat po. Ngayon nabanggit rin po yung Oplan Romanov. Sabi po ni Atty. Lotoc, Ang alam niya ay banta ito sa presidente at pamilya nila na nagmula kay Mayor Sebastian Duterte. Sa kabilang banda, ayon naman kay Princess Maui, ay banta daw po yan sa buhay ni vicepresidente at pamilyang Duterte. Pareho po ba yang iniimbestigahan ng NBI?

04:18:49.710 --> 04:19:57.680
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang alam ko po, na-cover na po ng NBI noon yung imbestigasyon doon sa allegation na yung Oplan Romanov ay banta sa Vice Presidente dahil nagpadala nga po ng subpoena kay Princess Maui at kay Vice President. Subalit, unfortunately, hindi po yata sila dumalo diyan. Pero nung iyan po ay aming sinusuri din, yung binabanggit ninyo po na Romanov, I think that was the January 18, 2024 na pahayag po ni Mayor Baste Duterte kung saan sinabi niya: ‘Let me tell you this, Mr. Bongbong Marcos.’ Hindi ko lang po maano yung exact words, but I remember that 'Before you go to sleep, remember the Romanovs and the Mussolinis and what happened to the Marcos family in 1986.' Yun po yung nakita nati na isa na nagli-link po diyan sa Romanov. Kaya recently narinig ko rin po yung dating director na sinasabi niya na ang Oplan Romanov ay tunay na banta sa pamilya ng mga Marcoses at hindi po kay Vice President Sara Duterte.

04:20:01.400 --> 04:20:13.910
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So base po sa imbestigasyon ng NBI, ang Oplan Romanov po ba ay banta sa buhay ng Presidente o sa buhay ng Vice Presidente?

04:20:17.160 --> 04:20:24.940
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Kaya po merong kaming task force kasama po yan sa aming continuing surveillance at active investigation po.

04:20:33.710 --> 04:20:41.840
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: May actionable intelligence po ba ang NBI na posibleng patuloy pa rin ang panganib sa buhay ng Presidente doon sa linyang iyon ng inyong imbestigasyon?

04:20:41.980 --> 04:21:20.840
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po yan sapagkat... Pinanggit ko nga po kanina yung ginagamit sa National Threat Assessment Center po ng Secret Service ng Amerika, ay pumapasok po doon yung mga observation na iyan. At katunayan po, lalo pang lumawig o lumawak yung mga banta sa presidente, namin pong namumonitor. Pati po ang mga ordinaryong tao ngayon ay napakadali po na magbigay ng banta. At para sa amin po, hindi lang naman po yung banta sa ating Pangulong ang aming binabandayan kundi yung pong bandayan natin ang kaligtasan ng ating mga kababayan at isiguraduhin natin na ang democratic process po ay umiiral sa atin base sa ating pong Constitution po.

04:21:21.580 --> 04:21:32.360
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: At sa kabilang banda naman po, may actionable intelligence din po ba ang NBI na may totoong banta sa buhay naman ng Vice Presidente?

04:21:32.580 --> 04:21:56.610
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa ngayon po, Hindi po namin tinitingnan kung totoo may actionable intel, pero base po sa aming mandato, kasama po sa mandato namin na proteksyonan po ang siguridad ng Pangulo, ng Vice Presidente, ng Senate President, ng Speaker of the House at Chief Justice. Kaya kung wala man pong task force, tuloy-tuloy naman po ang aming pagpamonitor dito.

04:21:56.970 --> 04:22:11.480
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pero sa ngayon, kung isusuma po natin: may actionable intelligence na may patuloy na panganib sa buhay ng Presidente, pero wala pang actionable intelligence na may banta din naman sa buhay ng Vice Presidente?

04:22:13.640 --> 04:22:23.820
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Malinaw po iyon sapagkat lumabas lang naman po iyon doon sa sinasabi nitong si Princess Maui.

04:22:23.830 --> 04:22:24.870
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Witness. Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

04:22:24.880 --> 04:22:36.670
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator-Judge Risa Hontiveros. Next to interject and make his interventions would be our Senate President, Sherwin Gatchalian. He is recognized. You have two minutes, sir. You may proceed when you're ready.

04:22:36.210 --> 04:22:37.770
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Maraming salamat, Mr. Presiding Officer.

04:22:39.590 --> 04:22:50.940
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Tama po ba, Director Matibag, na after one year and eight months, wala pang nakikita ang NBI na nakontratang papatay?

04:22:51.710 --> 04:22:56.170
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala po pong specific na personalidad. Wala pang specific na nakikita.

04:22:56.290 --> 04:23:06.430
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Pero kanina narinig ko sa inyong testimonya, may sinabi kayong hindi banta kundi isang plano talaga. So may plano.

04:23:06.990 --> 04:23:32.840
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yun po ang base sa mismong pahayag ng ating pong vicepresidente na siya ay kinausap at yung kinausap niya ay pumayag para patayin po ang mga taong nabanggit. Para sa akin po, this is actually a public confession na dahil sa sinabi niyang ito, nalagay po sa alanganin hindi lamang po. Ang siguridad ng presidente kundi po ang ating pambansyang siguridad.

04:23:32.980 --> 04:23:43.380
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Sino ang kaplano niya? Kung magpaplano, obviously may kasama siya sa pagpaplano. Sino na ang natukoy ng NBI na kasama sa pagpaplano?

04:23:43.580 --> 04:23:56.270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yan na po yung binabanggit namin na persons of interest based on the open source intel and the human intel po na binabato po sa amin na yan po ay reported po sa atin ng Atting pong task force na itinayo po.

04:23:56.390 --> 04:24:03.850
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Itong persons of interest kasama sa pagpaplano at inamin sa inyo na merong pagpaplanong ginagawa para pumatay?

04:24:03.990 --> 04:24:07.930
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Meron po silang impormasyon na magtuturo po dito sa pagpaplanong ito po.

04:24:07.930 --> 04:24:10.470
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Hindi sila 'yung kasama sa pagpaplanong pumatay?

04:24:10.650 --> 04:24:11.650
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa ngayon po...

04:24:11.650 --> 04:24:13.210
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Magtuturo lang sila?

04:24:13.330 --> 04:24:20.910
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Doon po sa persons of interest, meron po kami kinukonsidera doon na maaaring siya po ang kausap mismo ng Vice President.

04:24:20.910 --> 04:24:28.140
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: At anong ebidensya ang magpapatunay na kasama siya sa pagpaplano o kaya niyang ituro 'yung pagpaplano?

04:24:28.660 --> 04:24:43.680
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yan po ang ating kukunin na informasyon pa sa ating mga persons of interest na ating sinusurveillance. Katunayan po as we speak, tuloy-tuloy po yung ating pakikipag-usap. Pati po doon sa mga malalapit sa taong aking binabanggit. So

04:24:43.680 --> 04:24:45.640
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: So tuloy-tuloy pa ngayon ang inyong investigation?

04:24:46.320 --> 04:24:46.660
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

04:24:46.780 --> 04:25:03.330
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Ngayon nakita ko na bumuo kayo ng task force. At task force? Temporary in nature lang yan, di ba? Kailangan matatapos ang inyong investigasyon? Dahil nga nasabi ko one year and eight months na ito, ngayon may bagong task force. So kailang matatapos itong investigation?

04:25:04.350 --> 04:25:24.940
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ito po ay matatapos finally pag atin pong na-locate specifically ang taong kausap ng Vice Presidente. At ito naman pong task force, bukod po sa seguridad ng Presidente, we are also guarding po na walang gulo, na yung mga destabilization ay atin ding mab...

04:25:24.950 --> 04:25:51.590
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Pero kailan matatapos yung investigation para matukoy kung sino yung nakontrata? Do you have a time frame based doon sa pag-uusap ninyo dito sa persons of interest ninyo? Kasi, like I said, November of 2024 ito, may bagong task force ngayon. But in your opinion, gusto ko kasing malaman: malapit na ba o malayo pa?

04:25:51.070 --> 04:26:05.440
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I cannot give the exact time, but the task force was established on April 16, and it's doing a great progress po. So sa palagay ko po, malapit na rin natin itong mahanap, itong taong ating tinutukoy.

04:26:05.450 --> 04:26:10.030
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Can you give me an explanation on yung, quote-unquote, ‘great progress’?

04:26:11.010 --> 04:26:18.410
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Marami pong report na pumasok po sa atin at may mga pangalan po talaga na na-identify. Natin pong pinupuntahan po.

04:26:18.590 --> 04:26:29.470
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: And can you give me a time frame kung within 3 months, 6 months matutukoy na itong kakontrata?

04:26:30.440 --> 04:26:33.030
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Can you give me a time frame? An indicative time frame?

04:26:33.040 --> 04:26:51.630
Atty. Melvin Matibag: As we go on to the progress, probably po within three to six months magkakaroon po tayo ng mas malinaw na data tungkol po dito. But in three to six months, matutukoy na natin yung nakontrata. Yun po ang ating inaasahan.

04:26:51.640 --> 04:27:11.710
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Okay. In the meantime, nasabi ninyo kanina na merong kinetic force. Ito, ina-assume ko na may naiimpluwensyahan. Sino na ho ang nakausap ninyo na naimpluwensyahan tungkol dito sa mga sinasabi ng Vice President at yung iba pa?

04:27:11.860 --> 04:27:31.080
Atty. Melvin Matibag: May mga ilan na po kaming pinuntahan. At katunayan may ilan na po kaming sinampahan na rin ng mga kaso. At yung mga nagbanta through social media ay atin na rin pong nakausap. At yung iba naman po sa ngayon ay kasalukuyang humaharap po sa investigation po. Last

04:27:31.080 --> 04:27:33.980
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: question. So itong dahil sa kanilang pananalita,

04:27:56.180 --> 04:27:56.720
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Maraming

04:27:56.720 --> 04:27:57.760
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: salamat, Mr. President.

04:28:02.080 --> 04:28:08.000
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Will Senator Judge Allan make an interjection or will he make a manifestation regarding another matter?

04:28:10.160 --> 04:28:19.320
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Then, the Presiding Officer will first recognize Senator Judge Aquino for his interjections and interventions. You may proceed, sir. When you're ready, you have two minutes. Thank you,

04:28:19.340 --> 04:28:22.500
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Mr. Presiding Officer. Very quickly lang, Director Matibag.

04:28:24.020 --> 04:29:01.280
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Kapag sinasabi kasing bukas pa ang isang investigasyon, posibleng meron, posibleng wala. Diba? Pero ito po, just one question. Sa inyo pong professional assessment, anong porsyento, what percentage is the probability na meron ngang nakausap na tao ang vicepresidente para gawin yung mga pagpatay? Sa inyo pong assessment. Hindi nyo pa po masasabi. May kailangan pa kayong ilang buwan. Pero sa inyong assessment po ba, anong porsyento po na meron talagang nakausap ang vicepresident?

04:29:01.590 --> 04:29:07.530
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Base po mismo sa pahayag ng Vice President, nakasisiguro po na merong kinausap.

04:29:07.610 --> 04:29:09.470
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Anong percentage po? Seventy percent?

04:29:09.490 --> 04:29:19.890
Atty. Melvin Matibag: One hundred percent po, sapagkat siya na mismo ang nagsabi ng kanyang plano, na siya'y may kinausap na papatay at pumayag 'yung papatay sa kanilang pag-uusap.

04:29:19.950 --> 04:29:21.270
Sen. Paolo Benigno “Bam” Aquino: Maraming salamat, Mr. President.

04:29:23.000 --> 04:29:29.820
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Cayetano Allan is recognized for his interjections.

04:29:30.320 --> 04:29:59.940
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Before that, on the same point of Senator Baum, may I just manifest that I have submitted, presiding officer, Mr. Senate President, written continuing objection to the ruling on the presiding officer dated 20 July 2026 on the subpoena. But according to the journal service, journal service, it will not be included in the journal. May I move that it be included in the records? In the records, whatever is...

04:30:04.540 --> 04:30:15.930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It will definitely be in the record and transcript. We will see what we can do about the journal. Can we get back to you? Because there's a technical difficulty.

04:30:15.940 --> 04:30:26.140
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: under an impression until today. That's why hinabol ko ng 531, then nilagay ko na lang possible supplemental. But whatever is more convenient for the clerk of court.

04:30:26.340 --> 04:30:30.540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The chair will entertain a motion to reconsider the approval of the journal earlier.

04:30:35.960 --> 04:30:36.520
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: May

04:30:36.520 --> 04:30:45.400
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: I move that we reconsider approval of journal just so that we can include what we agreed on yesterday which is the written objection.

04:30:45.880 --> 04:31:28.200
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: There is a motion to reconsider the approval of the journal of yesterday July 20, 2026 in order to include as part of the journal the written manifestation of Senator Judge Alan Cayetanas. We have done so. With respect to Senator Judges Villanueva, Marcos, Go, Villar Camille, and Legarda. Absent any objections, the motion is approved. Journal is reconsidered. And the insertion of the manifestation of the Honorable Cayetano is so included, so ordered. Thank you, dear colleagues. Would you like to complete the process and move for the approval of the journal now? We move the approval

04:31:28.200 --> 04:31:30.760
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: with the amendment, not an insertion.

04:31:31.960 --> 04:31:38.740
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The journal is approved as amended by inserting the manifestation of Senator Judge Alan Cayetano. Is there any objection?

04:31:40.360 --> 04:31:43.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Hearing none, the same is approved. Sands, the reading of the same.

04:31:44.200 --> 04:32:05.130
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Mr. Presiding Officer, just one point. Just to make a manifestation. Yes, Mr. President. I just wanted to put on record that this representation is not objecting to the ruling of the chair yesterday and that the only reason why I wanted to put into the records my manifestation with regard to the ruling of the chair. Just to put on record. Thank you.

04:32:05.930 --> 04:32:12.050
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Duly noted. Senator-Judge Cayetano may proceed with his interjections. He has two minutes. You may proceed, sir, when you're ready.

04:32:12.170 --> 04:32:41.450
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Good afternoon, Mr. Witness, Director, Atty. Matibag, schoolmate. Good afternoon, sir, Your Honor. Just on that point ni Senator Bam, I understand as a law enforcer, as an investigator, you have to take all threats seriously. I'll ask you the same questions I asked the two NBI officers, and I do understand they were not under your supervision during that time dahil doon pa sila kay Director Santiago.

04:32:43.540 --> 04:32:57.140
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: I won't ask all the questions, but you did review the whole video or just the portions relevant to the statement of the vice president na no joke, no joke, yung November 23?

04:32:57.760 --> 04:33:04.320
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Your Honor, naponood ko po yung video but you're correct, I focused mainly on the issue that is being understood. So

04:33:04.320 --> 04:33:04.480
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: simple

04:33:04.480 --> 04:33:04.940
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: question,

04:33:05.300 --> 04:33:28.550
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: paano naging process kung anong parts ng video at ng statement niya ang paniniwalaan mo or ng task force? So, it's not personal. I mean, if you were in the task force or as you said, you created the task force now at duty nyo yung safety ng high government officials, anong process nyo kung anong parts ng video ang paniniwalaan nyo at hindi? Ng statements niya, what I meant. Well,

04:33:28.770 --> 04:33:57.030
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang ginawa po natin diyan, doon po mismo sa konteksto ng kanyang sinabi na humanap siya ng papatay at inutos niya na papatayin ang tatlong individual. Yun po ay pumayag yung papatay at sinabi pa niya, ‘No joke.’ Doon pa lamang po ay nakita na natin yung ating hinahanap na mga pwede niyang pananagutan po sa batas.

04:33:57.040 --> 04:34:45.150
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Well, as an appointee of this government, as a lawyer, as an NBI director, I see your point and I get that. But what I meant is that before that statement, sabi kasi niya, ‘Kung papatayin ako,’ I mean the record will bear out naman yung eksaktong sinabi niya. So this is my paraphrase. But ang pagkaintindi ko sa sinabi niya, kung papatayin ako, ito yung tatlong papatayin mo. And ang impression ko, pinagbibintangan niya yung tatlo na may plot against her. So yun ang tanong ko doon sa two previous NBI directors. If you're going to believe that she contracted or talked to—may kausap siya—and papapatay yung tatlo, will you not believe the previous, nung sinabi niyang, ‘Kung ako naman ang papatayin’?

04:34:46.190 --> 04:35:12.510
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Hindi po ganun sapagkat ang tinignan na nga po natin ay yung kanyang mismong pagbabanta. At nasa amin po sa ngayon yung aking pong task force na nag-iimbestiga ay malinaw po na ang tinitingnan ay kung ano na ang nangyari dahil doon sa pagbabanta. At sinasabi nga po namin dahil po doon sa pagbabanta, ito po ay umabot na doon na po sa level na ang national security na taya na po na kumpormisyon na.

04:35:16.080 --> 04:35:19.980
Atty. Melvin Matibag: In the same video, she

04:35:19.980 --> 04:35:51.390
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: mentioned massive corruption. But wala pa dyan kasi yung maya kayo speech at flood control investigation. So, same question, Director. Naintindihan ko, yun yung pinaniwalaan niyo. May kausap siya, no joke, no joke. Pero ang question ko, paano yung proseso niyo or anong naging thinking niyo na etong... Papapatay yung presidente, pinaniniwalaan ko. Pero etong siya ang papatayin, hindi ko paniniwalaan. At etong grap and corruption, hindi ko rin paniniwalaan. What's the process there?

04:35:51.970 --> 04:36:34.450
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, ang proseso po dyan, ang tinignan naman natin, doon po sa pagbabantanya, kung sa grave threat po yung pag-uusapan natin, alam naman po natin na yung threat na yan is absolute. Dahil nandoon naman po yung elemento eh. Doon naman po sa sinasabi namin na tuloy-tuloy na pag-iimbestiga, Ito nga po ay umabot na sa level na naapekto ng national security. We take into context yung mismong sinabi niya na meron siyang kinausap at yung kanyang kinausap ay pumayag. Yung po kanyang sinasabi na kung papatayin ako, that is supposed to be na statement niya sa aming pananaw just to cover yung kanyang pagsasabi na siya ay may kinausap para patayin ang ating Pangulo.

04:36:34.920 --> 04:37:13.030
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Okay, I won't argue with you. 'Yun yung proseso ninyo. But in the meantime, there were three statements: massive corruption; kung papatayin siya, patayin yung tatlo kung papatayin siya. So, focusing doon sa patayin yung tatlo kung papatayin siya. In the meantime, tumotoo yung massive corruption; lumabas afterwards, 'di ba? So, just one other point. At the beginning of the prosecution's questions to you, and I think the defense had a question about what can you investigate. Can you repeat your answer? As the NBI director, can the NBI investigate—did you say all crimes or yung mga crime?

04:37:13.040 --> 04:37:44.230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Lahat po ng mga pumapasok sa amin na mga krimen ay amin pong puwedeng imbestigahan motu proprio. Ganoon din po yung mga krimen na meron pong nagrereklamo, na araw-araw may pumupunta sa aming tanggapan para magreklamo. Ito po yung aming iniimbestigahan, at meron din pong mga iniimbestigahan kami na inutos po ng Department of Justice. And by the very nature, under the Constitution po ng Office of the Ombudsman, they can delegate the National Bureau of Investigation to—

04:37:44.240 --> 04:37:48.910
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: So, as a general rule, you can investigate any crime motu proprio?

04:37:48.920 --> 04:38:00.430
Atty. Melvin Matibag: More than the investigation of the crime is also the protection of our nationals. Saka po, siyempre, siguraduhing napo-promote ang ating demokrasya, hindi nakukompromiso.

04:38:00.440 --> 04:38:04.230
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Yes. But sa investigation lang. So you can investigate any crime?

04:38:04.240 --> 04:38:05.270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

04:38:05.280 --> 04:38:11.480
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Yeah. Isn't that against Republic Act No. 10867, the statute that gives you power?

04:38:13.490 --> 04:39:46.150
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Reorganizing and Modernizing the National Bureau of Investigation. Sabi dito sa inyong Section 4, the NBI shall have the following powers and functions. Undertake and investigate the detection of crimes and offenses enumerated under Section 5. Section 5 My enumeration, human trafficking cases in all airports, extrajudicial, extralegal killings committed by state security forces against media practitioners' activities, killings of justices and judges, violation of 10.01.75, otherwise known as Cyber Crime Prevention Act, cases against interagency graph coordinating counsel, and violations of the anti-dummy law. Tapos, cases involving threats Security assaults against persons of the President, Vice President, Senate President, Speaker of the House, Chief Justices. Walang Congressmen, Senators, unlike judges lahat. Transnational crimes pursuant to existing international agreements, identification of dead victims in case of mass fatalities, incidents caused by natural disaster, and violation of commercial, economic, financial, white-collar crimes. Daka dyan yung law. So, exclusive yung enumeration. Then, provided, however, if that the President or Secretary of Justice may direct the NBI to undertake investigation of any crime when public interest so requires. So, hindi ba limited ang pwede niyong investigahan except that ang DOJ at President ang pwede mag-atas? That's my last question.

04:39:46.410 --> 04:39:49.490
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes. Kindly wind up. Witness may answer.

04:39:49.650 --> 04:40:04.610
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes. Yung pong ating listahan na yan, tama po, nandiyan dyan. Subalit hindi naman po sinasabi na nalilimitad dyan ang aming pong pag-iimbestiga sapagkat malino po ang mandato ng NBI that we are the primary investigating body. Yun lamang nga po.

04:40:13.460 --> 04:40:13.940
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Director,

04:40:18.420 --> 04:40:29.540
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: if that's your interpretation, that goes against what they taught us in law school, na pag-exclusive yung enumeration, you cannot add. And at the end of the enumeration of Section 5, nakalagay nga dito,

04:40:51.310 --> 04:40:59.970
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa pagkat na we have also our primary role to make sure that law and order is being promoted through the NBI din po.

04:41:03.580 --> 04:41:13.500
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Later or tomorrow, since I believe Atty. Matibag, Director Matibag, forgive me, will still be here for the continuation of cross. Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo, thereafter.

04:41:15.750 --> 04:41:17.930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Pangilinan.

04:41:20.570 --> 04:41:24.550
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo, you have, I believe, one question, right?

04:41:26.070 --> 04:41:27.570
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Actually, two questions, Your Honor.

04:41:27.690 --> 04:41:29.650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed, sir. You have two minutes, actually.

04:41:29.810 --> 04:41:42.850
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Naku, na-stress na ako kanina, limang minuto ako doon. But anyway, going back to Ronel Mas, What was the justification of the NBI back then when Mr. Ronell Mas was arrested without warrant?

04:41:43.210 --> 04:41:52.570
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, they consider po that the threat is live and alam niyo nga po yung sinasabi na lahat po ng threat ay hindi po, ito po ay sinuseryoso. So

04:41:52.570 --> 04:41:52.730
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: may

04:41:52.730 --> 04:41:53.170
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: nag-order

04:41:53.170 --> 04:41:55.430
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: sa naarestuin si Ronell Mas?

04:41:55.430 --> 04:42:01.770
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I don't have that recollection. Hindi ko po alam but it was, the arrest was made by the regional office po of Region 1 po.

04:42:01.890 --> 04:42:09.240
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So would you admit now... Na illegal yung ginawa ng NBI noon na pag-aresto kay Ronell Mas na walang warrant?

04:42:09.700 --> 04:42:15.780
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, si Ronell Mas po was released precisely for the reason na meron pong lapses po doon sa procedure.

04:42:16.100 --> 04:42:29.960
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Would you also consider na, the fact na merong ginawang pagbabanta si Baste Duterte na similar dito kay Ronell Mas, dapat umaksyon din 'yung NBI tulad ng pag-aksyon nila sa isang guro?

04:42:30.330 --> 04:42:52.230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Kaya katunayan yan nga po yung aking binabanggit na tuloy-tuloy po yung investigation sapagkat alam nyo po yung warrantless arrest lesson nga po dyan kay Romel Marcian na dapat po kasi immediate po yung pong pag-aresto. Pag yan po ay lumipas na eh hindi na po tayo pwedeng mag-aresto under the law sapagkat papasok po ito sa illegal arrest po.

04:42:52.290 --> 04:43:10.150
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Last na lamang, so make a comparison ngayon. Bakit yung isang guro na nagbanta kay dati pangung Duterte agad inaresto? At bakit itong isang vice president na nagbanta kay Pangulong Bongbong Marcos hindi inaresto ng NBI?

04:43:11.610 --> 04:43:21.430
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I can only second guess po na maaaring may pagkakaiba po ng proseso o tinitingnan po ang administrasyon ng panahon na iyon at ng panahon po ngayon.

04:43:21.450 --> 04:43:22.190
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Maraming salamat po.

04:43:22.960 --> 04:43:29.960
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator-Judge Raffy Tulfo. Senator-Judge Pangilinan is recognized. You may proceed with your intervention, sir. You have two minutes.

04:43:30.240 --> 04:43:48.710
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Magandang gabi, ginoong direktor. Kanina tinatanong sa inyo yung usapin ng trust rating, na mas mataas yung trust rating ng Vice President kaysa sa President.

04:43:50.770 --> 04:44:03.560
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Bilang abogado, Ang tinanong sa iyo ito kanina. May kinalaman ba ang approval sa trust? Kung mas mataas ang trust rating, ibig sabihin wala nang betrayal of the public trust?

04:44:04.000 --> 04:44:19.340
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, wala po. Sapagkat sabi ko nga sa akin pong pananaw, sa akin din pong kaunting eksperyensa bilang isang political advisor din po, eh yung ating mga survey is only a snapshot.

04:44:35.050 --> 04:44:49.470
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Pagkakaroon po tayo ng problema sapagkat ang mangyayari sa atin dyan, yung tinitingnan pala natin ay yung numero. At without accusing anyone, alam naman natin there are surveys that can be manipulated po.

04:44:49.770 --> 04:45:03.630
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: But having said that, kaya ako lang tinanong yun kasi baka yung mga nakikinig nating mga kababayan ay malito dahil hindi ba tamang sabihin na iba yung trust rating, iba yung betrayal of the public trust?

04:45:03.970 --> 04:46:15.310
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po. Yung trust rating po ay base sa numero dahil sa survey. Yung betrayal of public trust, malinaw naman po iyan na nakasaad sa Constitution na ito ay isang basehan ng impeachment. At saan po pumapasok ang betrayal of public trust? Pag meron ka pong ginawa na pag-violate, not necessarily criminal. Hindi kailangan ng conviction. Pag tinignan natin yung discussion po ng ating Constitutional Committee nang ginawa iyan, binabanggit nga po diyan yung betrayal of public trust: yung hindi mo pagtupad sa iyong oath of office. That will qualify as a betrayal of public trust. In other words, negative yung trust rating mo o 100% yung trust rating mo, base sa batas, base sa Constitution, pwede kang ma-convict whether negative or positive trust rating; pwede ka pa ring ma-convict o ma-acquit depende sa ebidensya sa usapin ng betrayal of the public trust. Wala pong kinalaman ang survey on the trust rating kundi kung ano po ang ebidensya na ipinasok po sa ating impeachment court. Maraming salamat.

04:46:16.320 --> 04:46:25.800
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Senator Judge Pia Cayetano is recognized for her interjections and interventions. You may proceed ma'am when you are ready and you have two minutes.

04:46:53.270 --> 04:46:55.430
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: For the prosecution, do you consider Lascañas a witness for you?

04:46:55.440 --> 04:47:23.760
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: With all respect, Your Honor, the purpose of the testimony is to present what transpired during the investigation of the Special Task Force. As to whether or not what probative value it holds, it is not part actually of the decision of the prosecution. What we are intending to do here is to present only what happened during the investigation of the NBI, Your Honor.

04:47:34.030 --> 04:48:21.450
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Mr. Presiding Officer, the Rules of Evidence are very clear. You either present a witness who provides your testimony or you present a document. And in terms of documents, Rule 132, Section 19 says there are two classes of documents: public documents and private documents. Included in public documents are documents acknowledged before a notary public. Yung pinakitang document is not acknowledged by a notary public. Pwede naman din ang private documents—that's the other class—if it can be shown and authenticated in any of the following manner: the person saw the document executed or written. Nakita ba ng witness mo na sinulat iyon? Nakita ba niya?

04:48:22.380 --> 04:48:23.880
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, we can...

04:48:22.960 --> 04:48:26.710
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Please answer my question.

04:48:26.720 --> 04:48:28.150
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: No, Your Honor.

04:48:28.160 --> 04:48:42.950
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: The next manner of authenticating: by evidence of the genuineness of the signature or handwriting of the maker. The defense said walang original signature doon. Do you disagree with that?

04:48:49.070 --> 04:48:49.910
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: No, Your Honor.

04:48:50.050 --> 04:48:52.390
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, so simple lang, Mr. Presiding Officer.

04:48:54.890 --> 04:49:53.680
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: They're trying to prove something by showing a document that any law student, even yung mga kababayan natin na nakikinig na ngayon na ang daming alam sa procedure, will tell you na hindi acceptable iyon. And with all due respect, katulad din nung kahapon na humingi ako ng payo sa inyo, again, I will not name names. We had a discussion in caucus na you cannot unsee what you see; you cannot unhear what you hear.

04:49:56.200 --> 04:49:59.110
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: May I respond, Your Honor?

04:49:59.120 --> 04:50:00.960
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Not really. I don't believe there was a question.

04:50:00.970 --> 04:50:05.030
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Because I already asked you the questions and you had a chance to respond.

04:50:05.040 --> 04:50:05.910
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Yes, I—

04:50:05.920 --> 04:50:10.270
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: There was no question posed. I was telling the lead prosecutor.

04:50:10.280 --> 04:50:14.560
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: I move to my next point, Mr. Presiding Officer.

04:50:18.660 --> 04:50:52.110
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Our jurisprudence is very clear. A witness must be competent and credible. Hindi ko na babasahin lahat yung jurisprudence natin diyan dahil kumpleto na yung record natin diyan. But there is also included in our rules, Rule 132 on the Rules of Evidence. And I'll read it: a witness may be impeached by the party against whom he or she was called by contradictory evidence, by evidence that his or her general reputation for truth, honesty, or integrity is bad.

04:50:54.560 --> 04:51:00.280
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Or by evidence that he or she has made at other times statements inconsistent with his or her present testimony.

04:51:01.820 --> 04:51:12.820
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: So this is the rules, no siguro we can, well I'm reading the rules so we can take notice of this that this is what our rules say and I don't think anyone will contradict that.

04:51:16.510 --> 04:51:18.610
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Again, there are lots of cases supporting this.

04:51:21.430 --> 04:51:22.930
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: So, I

04:51:32.560 --> 04:51:37.780
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: just want to point out, Mr. President, that just looking for my notes.

04:52:02.310 --> 04:52:10.410
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry with the indulgences of the body. I'm just looking for my notes because I want to be accurate in the next statement that I'm going to read into the record.

04:52:30.150 --> 04:52:33.950
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: If the lady cannot locate it, she may avail of her time again tomorrow since Director Matibag and the counsel for the parties will be here tomorrow.

04:52:33.960 --> 04:53:02.910
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Pwede naman, but if you give me a few more seconds, I might be able to dispose of this issue, Mr. President—Mr. Presiding Officer. Okay, I won't delay. I can paraphrase it, but I think it would be best if I look at the record, so I will just avail.

04:53:02.920 --> 04:53:33.710
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The Presiding Officer will give the lady first crack at interventions by a Senator-Judge tomorrow after the cross-examination of counsel for respondent. Since Director Matibag will be here again tomorrow for the continuation of cross-examination, the interjections and interventions of the other Senator-Judges may proceed again after the cross-examination, redirect, and recross, if any.

04:53:49.310 --> 04:53:59.090
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Your Honor, aside from the Las Cañas document, we would also like to request a copy of the AO number 11. Just for reference, Your Honor, to be used as AO number 11.

04:53:59.470 --> 04:54:06.790
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The prosecutor is directed to furnish—

04:54:08.800 --> 04:54:10.110
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: Can we do that after the proceedings, sir?

04:54:10.120 --> 04:54:21.690
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Within the day after the proceedings, a copy of AO No. 11, signed by Director Matibag, dated, if I'm not mistaken, April 16, 2026.

04:54:23.910 --> 04:54:26.370
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Any other points you want to raise, lead prosecutor?

04:54:28.300 --> 04:54:32.320
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: It appears that there is a standing subpoena for

04:54:32.320 --> 04:54:36.950
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ms. Marivic-Pareja of

04:54:36.950 --> 04:54:49.750
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Legislative Archive. We manifested yesterday that we have yet to determine when we will be presenting this witness. We will act

04:54:49.750 --> 04:54:53.690
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: on these at the proper time. This will be part of the chair's ruling before we adjourn.

04:54:53.750 --> 04:55:06.790
Rep. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: May I inquire, Your Honor, if tomorrow we will be able to conclude the testimony of witness Director Matibag, whether or not we will be proceeding to present the first witness for confidential fund, Your Honor.

04:55:06.890 --> 04:55:09.870
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The court will address that in a bit before we adjourn, counsel.

04:55:11.460 --> 04:55:13.440
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Any other points, counsel or the respondent?

04:55:15.240 --> 04:55:16.160
Atty. Mark C. Vinluan: No more, Your Honor.

04:55:17.820 --> 04:55:20.620
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Court will now dispose of some administrative matters.

04:55:22.500 --> 04:56:09.840
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: We are in receipt of a request for subpoena at testificandum addressed to Ms. Marivic Pareja as well as subpoena at testificandum addressed to Mr. Roderick C. Wamil and Ms. Aileen May Del Ocampo, both from the Commission on Audit. The Chair, the Presiding Officer, the first action on these requests for subpoena and will act on them at the proper time and in due time. In regard to the subpoena, ad testificandum, and do sestecom issued to Ms. Violeta Constantino and Ms. Nanita Camposano, the Chair in the meantime recalls the subpoenas issued to them.

04:56:11.500 --> 04:56:31.530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Without prejudice to reissuing the subpoena at a later time for a later date. Para po sa kalaman, ang dalawang sinabpoena ng Senado nito bilang impeachment court na si Ginang o Binibining Violeta Constantino, Ginang o Binibining Nanita Campuzano, hindi niya po kailangan magpunta dito sa hukuman bukas.

04:56:33.450 --> 04:56:49.750
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Binabawi pong pansamantala ng hukumang ito ang sapinang in-issue para sa inyo. At mag-i-issue na lamang po kami ng panibagong sapina kung kailan po kayo kinakailangan magpunta o magtungo dito sa impeachment court sa Senado. What is the pleasure of Senator Judge Zubiri?

04:56:51.500 --> 04:57:00.990
Sen. Juan Miguel “Migz” F. Zubiri: Thank you very much, Presiding Officer. Just want to ask a question. You are withdrawing the subpoena because you feel that we might not take them up tomorrow, is that correct?

04:57:00.990 --> 04:57:02.370
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, that is correct, Your Honor.

04:57:02.710 --> 04:57:09.920
Sen. Juan Miguel “Migz” F. Zubiri: Habang pa ba ito kay witness Atiba? You mean we cannot take it up tomorrow?

04:57:10.340 --> 04:57:17.020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I would think so. That was pursuant to a discussion with both counsel for the parties earlier. So

04:57:17.020 --> 04:57:20.120
Sen. Juan Miguel “Migz” F. Zubiri: we're looking at taking up that article on Monday?

04:57:20.440 --> 04:57:22.340
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, that is correct, Your Honor. Okay.

04:57:22.400 --> 04:57:23.020
Sen. Juan Miguel “Migz” F. Zubiri: thank you, Your Honor.

04:57:23.760 --> 04:57:25.540
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Also, in regard to the trial,

04:57:27.790 --> 04:57:31.750
Sen. Juan Miguel “Migz” F. Zubiri: Tuesday pala po. Tuesday. Sorry. Monday is the sauna. So Tuesday.

04:57:31.950 --> 04:58:33.630
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Tuesday. I will discuss that too, Senator-Judge Zubiri. During caucus, the Senator-Judges agreed that next week there will be no trial on Monday, given that it's the State of the Nation Address of the President. There will be no trial on Tuesday to afford the minority the opportunity to prepare and deliver their Contra-SONA. So our next trial date, which we will clarify tomorrow, will be on July 29. On July 29, again as agreed in caucus by the senators and Senator-Judges, the new time of the trial will be from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m., and the session of the Senate will be at 4 p.m.

04:59:00.630 --> 04:59:10.590
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Henceforth, after that week in August, we will be conducting the trial from Monday to Wednesday from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m.

04:59:12.930 --> 04:59:15.430
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Council for the Parties are asked to take note.

04:59:17.440 --> 04:59:42.030
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: To avoid confusion, Director Matibag, we expect you to come back and be here again tomorrow, not at 10, but at 2 p.m., to continue with your testimony via the cross-examination, redirect or recross of counsel for the parties, and questions from the Senator-Judges. Without issuing a subpoena, Director Matibag, do we get your commitment to be here tomorrow?

04:59:42.040 --> 04:59:43.870
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes, Your Honor, gladly.

04:59:43.880 --> 05:00:01.640
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you very much. There being no other matters to be taken up and no other business to take up, the trial is hereby adjourned until tomorrow, Wednesday, July 22, at 2 p.m. in the afternoon.
